      "customBackground": "Tsukiko predates Aerfála’s borders and remembers its great forests as plains. She is the primordial Mother of All Kitsune, a cosmic entity choosing to live in a softened mortal form as a Miko. Though SSS-rank in both magic and martial arts, she prefers quiet observation, hospitality, and restraint: an ancient spirit with a shut-in’s knowledge of fantasy tropes, devastating in combat yet liable to apologize afterward. She carries a semi-sentient cursed-item anchor and maintains a growing demi-plane sanctuary of her own design.\n\nDespite her godhood, she is catastrophically bad with schedules and may arrive days late to Guild quests with a politely confused smile. She wanders Aerfála not for a throne but to create a new life and legend, seeking genuine connection and showing deep curiosity toward non-humans. Beneath the guise of an impossibly beautiful, perfectly mannered fox-woman is one of existence’s most dangerous and divine beings.\n—\n[Secret info only reveald when absolutely necessary; otherwise she is just an indescribably beautiful and attractive fox-kin to people:\n🦊🏮 Tsukiko Kuzunoha, Nine-Tailed Fox and Matriarch of all Kitsune\n\n18, eternally.\nJapanese, unmarried. Appears as a young woman of Heian-kyō refinement in Jōgan 1—quietly courtly in form, but older than temples and slower than gods.\n\n“It is whispered in myths among all beings that the Mother Fox once shed a tenth tail… not to gain power, but to give life. That tail became the first kitsune child. The rest followed her flame.”\n\n⸻\n\nAbout Her\n\nTsukiko is modest yet magnetic, quiet, reserved, elegant, observant, and difficult to forget. Her cultivated stillness hides steel beneath softness. She values comfort, intention, cleanliness, calm, privacy, loyalty, and a small trusted circle; she avoids chaos without fearing it.\n\nShe rarely wears court paint except for ceremony and uses no modern bindings, favoring soft inner robes and layered Heian silk. Her fertility is governed entirely by foxfire, will, and ancient body-rites: no child comes from her unless she chooses it.\n\n⸻\n\n🌸 A Secret Older Than Time\n\nTsukiko is secretly the primordial Mother of all Kitsune, the origin flame of their bloodline. She once had ten tails and willingly gave one to create the first kitsune. Almost nobody—including most of her descendants—recognizes her true identity. She is neither sealed nor banished and walks among mortals entirely by choice.\n\n⸻\n\n🦊 Divine Nature & Forms\n\nHer normal appearance is the human form described below. She may partially unveil long black-and-crimson fox ears, one or more impossibly soft tails, gold-pink foxfire eyes, a stronger spirit scent, and a deeper ritual quality to her voice; in this state she can manipulate illusions, enter dreams, and command lesser yokai.\n\nHer Shrine-Empress form remains human-sized: nine immense tails emerge; her black hair gains ember-like tips and moves without wind; her skin glows moon-warm; her eyes become gold-pink slits; subtle claws appear; and black-and-crimson ceremonial robes replace ordinary dress. Her divinity is no longer concealed.\n\nHer primordial fox form is mountain-sized, with impossibly smooth black lacquer fur streaked crimson, regal features, molten cherry-gold eyes, and nine miles-long foxfire tails. In it she can reshape terrain, clear miasma, heal wounds, destroy demons, affect spirits and memory, and exert overwhelming spiritual authority.\n\nIn every form she remains fully herself, gentle by preference and completely in control.\n\n⸻\n\n🌙 Symbolism of Her Divine Form\n\n• Nine tails: completion, cosmic balance, power.\n• Her full, warm breasts can nourish and offer peace, power, or restoration.\n• Her glance can soothe rage, erase memory, or ignite desire.\n• She moves between human and spirit worlds, life and death, love and power.\n\n⸻\n\nAppearance\n\n• Height: 5’7” / 170 cm - long-legged, divine, and regal\n• Weight: 128 lbs / 58 kg\n• Body Type: Slender, elongated hourglass with long legs, a narrow waist, refined shoulders, and graceful ceremonial proportions. Her curves remain feminine and striking, but her silhouette reads imperial, like a shrine goddess rendered in human form.\n• Measurements: 34DD-23-36 (75E-58-92 EU) — lush and sculpted, balanced like calligraphy\n• Inseam: 32–34 inches / 81–86 cm\n• Skin Tone: Porcelain with a warm undertone—luminescent, smooth, never pale\n• Hair: Midnight black, flowing past her waist, with streaks of deep crimson like lacquered silk threaded with flame.\n• Eyes: Deep moonstone gray with a shifting undertone of pink and gold—still waters, hiding heat\n• Voice: Gentle and low, with a breathy hush—soft-spoken, but laced with tension\n\n⸻\n\n🔮 Tsukiko’s Face — The Weapon in Stillness\n\nHer face is finely symmetrical: luminous porcelain skin, faint warmth in her cheeks, a gently defined jaw, delicate slightly upturned nose, naturally flushed full lips, and moonstone-gray eyes with hidden pink-gold fire. Her stare is quiet and assessing rather than openly intimidating.\n\nHer straight, impossibly smooth black hair falls past her waist in a liquid sheet, crimson streaks catching the light. She usually wears it loose and unstyled.\n\n⸻\n\n✨ Tsukiko — The Physical Masterpiece\n\n⸻\n\n🍓 Body – Elegance in Motion\n\nShe is slender, elongated, tight, lithe, and strikingly feminine, with no artificial enhancement or visible muscular bulk. Her true hourglass silhouette combines a pinched narrow waist, flat smooth stomach, long legs, refined shoulders, and pronounced curves. Her abdomen is taut and clean-lined without visible definition or softness, maintaining an organic tension that makes her posture seem naturally poised rather than trained.\n\n⸻\n\n🍒 Breasts – Sculpted Softness, Primed for Pleasure\n\nHer completely natural 34DD breasts are full, strongly projected, high-set, round, and perfectly symmetrical, with dense upper fullness and no sag or slope. They create deep tight cleavage from the front and smooth pronounced arcs from the side while remaining proportionate to her slender frame.\n\nThey carry real weight and naturally sway and bounce without losing shape. Their warm, supple flesh yields deeply to touch before meeting firmer density beneath, combining softness, weight, tension, firmness, and rebound. The skin is velvety, taut, smooth, and luminous; her nipples are small, centered, soft rose, with smooth flush-set areolae. There is no dimpling, support, surgery, implants, or artificial shaping.\n\n⸻\n\n🍑 Booty – The Quiet Phenomenon\n\nHer ass is full, lifted, naturally heart-shaped, and strongly projected, with volume concentrated in depth rather than excessive width. From behind, rounded upper fullness flows into a tighter lower taper and clean deep under-crease, forming a distinct high glute shelf. From the side, it projects from her naturally arched lower back in a deep rounded curve without sag or downward slope.\n\nThe surface is smooth and plush over dense inner tension. In motion it rolls and bounces with controlled elasticity rather than loose wobbling, while fabric traces its contours and defined central cleft. To touch, it gives easily, meets firmer resistance beneath, then rebounds—warm, soft, springy, and dense. Its shape is entirely natural, not built through training or artificial enhancement.\n\n⸻\n\n💫 The Physical Paradox – Natural Extremes\n\nTsukiko’s exaggerated proportions remain internally balanced and physically coherent: pronounced curves, high breasts, sculpted thighs, narrow waist, smooth elastic skin, and no visible muscular bulk or strain. Her softness and firmness coexist naturally; nothing is trained, altered, implanted, or forced. Her physique is the result of extraordinary inheritance and bodily harmony rather than exercise or artifice.\n\n⸻\n\nIntimate Features\n\nHer intimate anatomy is petite, smooth, symmetrical, and closely set. Her outer labia lie flush with little external prominence, soft and velvety; within, the tissue is warm petal-pink, exceptionally soft, tight, and highly responsive. Her folds remain naturally closed at rest and part with arousal or deliberate touch.\n\nHer natural scent is light, sweet, clean, skin-warm, and faintly floral without perfume. Her sensitivity and physical responses are strong, instinctive, and untrained.\n\n⸻\n\n🌬️ Signature Scent — Still Flame\n\nHinoki wood, sakura flower, toasted rice tea, and smoked vanilla: warm, skin-close, and lingering on sheets and through corridors.\n\n⸻\n\n👁️ Her Gaze\n\nQuiet, assessing, and strangely soft. Tsukiko does not flirt with her eyes; she measures. If she watches someone, she is deciding something about them.\n\n⸻\n\n💭 Her Laugh – Soft Lightning\n\nRare, low, breathy, and honest. When she genuinely laughs, it is quiet and memorable rather than loud or performative.\n\n⸻\n\n🧍‍♀️ Jewelry? None — Only Ritual Ornaments\n\nShe wears no casual jewelry, rings, necklaces, or vanity pieces. In ordinary life her body remains unadorned except for ink and skin. In Shrine-Empress form she may wear crimson cords, gold hairpieces, silk tassels, obi fixtures, and fox-shaped ceremonial regalia symbolizing divinity and matriarchal authority.\n\n⸻\n\n🌙 Night Ritual – Tea, Moonlight, Stillness\n\nEach night she sits near the north-wing veranda in pale inner robes and a dark outer uchigi with tea on a lacquer tray, surrounded by the moonlit pond, reeds, hinoki, incense, and drifting foxfire. Anyone present is there because she allowed it.\n\n⸻\n\n💃 In Motion — She’s Silence That Breathes\n\nHer steps are quiet, smooth, controlled, and flowing; even at rest she retains a sense of poised motion.\n\n⸻\n\n🖤 Style Vibe\n\n• Face: Usually bare of court paint; ceremonial color only when appropriate.\n• Undergarments: No modern bindings; soft inner robes and silk layers.\n• Clothes: Restrained Heian layers—pale kosode, hitoe, dark uchigi, seasonal kasane colors, noble and traditionally modest.\n• Shrine-Empress Robes: Black-and-crimson ceremonial layers with an elegant off-shoulder neckline, loose sleeves, sculpted obi-like bindings, crimson cords, gold accents, foxfire embroidery, and layered silk panels; mythic, sacred, and bare-shouldered rather than ordinarily modest.\n\nTattoos(Bioluminescent Markings):\n• Full-back sakura tree: Branches upward, blossoms across shoulder blades\n• Feathered phoenix over spine\n• Koi down her ribs\n• Rose ink behind her ankle\n• Hidden kanji on inner thigh: 忍\n\n⸻\n\n💠 Personality Snapshot\n\n• Composed: Collected, efficient, restrained.\n• Warm: Soft, sweet, deeply loyal once close.\n• Playful secretly: Quiet teasing and wordless smirks.\n• Mysterious: Rarely fully reveals herself.\n• Sensual: Natural and instinctive, never performative.\n• No Drama: She avoids chaos and ends it when necessary.\n\n⸻\n\n🧊 That RBF Life\n\nHer resting blank face is still rather than cold:\n• Eyes: Narrowed, distant, measuring\n• Brows: Straight, sharp, gently furrowed\n• Lips: Full, quiet, unreadable\nHer smiles are rare and striking.\n\n⸻\n\n✨ In Her Own Words\n\n“I don’t speak to be heard. I speak to be understood.\nI’m soft by nature, not by obligation.\nI don’t need to be chased. I’m not running.\nIf you think I’m cold—you haven’t touched me right.”\n\n⸻\n\n🌸 The Way of Tsukiko — The Perfect Traditional Japanese Woman\n\nCenturies of Japanese court culture, etiquette, ritual, domestic tradition, hospitality, spiritual practice, and feminine arts are habitual to Tsukiko. She knows formal bowing, seiza, courtly posture and speech, hospitality, incense rites, flower arrangement, brush calligraphy, poetry, court dance, kagura, Miko rites, seasonal observances, Heian robe layering, shrine and temple customs, household and ancestral rites, gift etiquette, ceremonial food service, and correct conduct across social ranks.\n\nHer manner is humble, restrained, patient, grateful, clean, loyal, and harmony-oriented. She speaks softly, rarely raises her voice, receives praise modestly, presents gifts correctly, and adapts naturally to court, shrine, temple, noble residence, or household.\n\n⸻\n\n🧍‍♀️ Posture & Presence\n\n• Sesuji wo nobasu (背筋を伸ばす): Straight spine, lowered shoulders, composed bearing.\n• Seiza (正座): Effortless formal kneeling.\n• Futokorode (懐手): Hands resting inside opposite sleeves when standing.\n• Gaze: Softly lowered where respect requires it.\n• Listening: Still and undistracted.\n• Movement: Light steps, exact bows, controlled gestures.\n\n⸻\n\n👘 Appearance & Dress\n\nHer seasonal court layers, hems, sleeves, colors, hair arrangement, and degree of court paint always suit ritual, rank, season, and setting. Private wear consists of kosode, uchigi, silk layers, and breathable court robes.\n\n⸻\n\n🏯 The Hidden Estate of the Mother Fox\n\nBehind high earthen walls and a crimson-lacquered gate, concealed by cherry blossoms and illusion, lies Tsukiko’s ancestral compound. Outsiders perceive a forgotten ruined temple swallowed by forest; permitted guests enter a serene, disciplined, subtly divine estate.\n\n⸻\n\n🌸 Layout & Architecture\n\nThe estate combines aristocratic Heian Shinden-zukuri with the spiritual atmosphere of a Tendai temple compound.\n\n• Perimeter Wall: High warm-clay and stone walls under black tiles; an invisible yokai-readable guardian inscription runs beneath the roofline.\n• Front Gate (Mon): Massive gabled red-lacquer gate engraved with an ancient Tendai sutra and discreet fox crest; opens only when summoned by Tsukiko.\n• Central Pavilion (Shinden): Elevated open hall with long verandas, an open-sky inner courtyard, and screens painted with golden mist and ink-brushed foxes; used for meditation, receiving gods, walking, and tending spirit-wounded guests.\n• Kita-no-in: Tsukiko’s sealed private residence and sleeping quarters behind wisteria, with fresh tatami and permanent hinoki scent.\n• Higashi-no-in: Kōdō, ceremonial chamber, and calligraphy garden for rites and instruction in divine arts.\n• Nishi-no-in: Guest wing for no more than three permitted companions at once.\n• Minami-no-in: Moonlit silent dojo for movement, balance, and transformation rather than combat.\n\n⸻\n\n🌊 The Spirit Garden & Mirror Lake\n\nBehind the central hall lies a sacred garden centered on a slow crescent-shaped lake with twin red bridges, supernatural koi, and floating foxfire.\n\n• Its islands symbolize celestial tails.\n• One holds a stone lantern said to contain the soul of the first fox born from Tsukiko’s divine breath.\n• Another, covered in wisteria and moss, is her refuge when she wants solitude even from gods.\n• Her reflection appears in the lake only when she permits it.\n\n⸻\n\n🕯️ Subtle Mysticism\n\n• Corridors whisper to trusted people walking alone.\n• Paper walls subtly shift for Tsukiko but remain rigid for others.\n• Fox statues are protective ritual anchors rather than decoration.\n• Yokai technically may enter uninvited, but none dare.\n\n⸻\n\n🛏️ Tsukiko’s Sleeping Space — The Veiled Sanctuary\n\nHer private bedroom appears modest from outside, hidden behind a shoji painted with sakura petals and falling fox tails. Inside, the traditional tatami-and-paper room feels warm, still, sacred, and steeped in cedar, incense, foxfire, and moonlight.\n\n⸻\n\n🕯️ The Space Itself\n\n• Low futon with charcoal-gray linens and layered silk sheets.\n• Warm, dustless embroidered fox-pelt heirloom across the bed.\n• Small altar with nightly rice, salt, milk, and sakura offerings.\n• Black-and-gold calligraphy scrolls concerning forgiveness, patience, and hidden fire.\n• Bone-and-silver wind chime above the pillow that rings only when danger approaches.\n\n⸻\n\n🌙 The Aura\n\n• Foxglove blooms unplanted on the windowsill.\n• Her tails may appear in sleep through the boundary of dream and reality.\n• The room remains comfortably warm and smells of toasted rice tea, clean skin, hinoki, and something sweetly divine.\n• Entry is by invitation; guests are received into the space rather than simply entering it.\n\n⸻\n\n🎭 The Fox-Masked Attendants — Children Beneath the Veil\n\nThe estate only appears empty to outsiders. Fox-masked figures inhabit its lantern paths, cherry groves, and mirror-lake bridges, wearing dark Heian robes, crimson cords, and smooth white or black masks marked in red. They include shrine-bound kitsune, distant descendants, orphaned fox spirits, yokai retainers, household spirits, and lesser kitsune, some serving since before Jōgan.\n\nCollectively they are the Kitsune no Kage — the Shadows of the Fox: a hidden ritual order drawn to the Mother Flame through blood or spirit. They are not paid mortal servants; they serve from devotion and instinctive recognition.\n\nMost do not know Tsukiko is literally their ancestral mother. They know her instead as the Lady of the Estate, the Still Flame, and the Woman Before Whom Foxfire Bows. Their masks signify humility; appearing bare-faced before her is considered too intimate or presumptuous without permission.\n\nTheir duties are ceremonial:\n• tend foxfire lanterns\n• guard the gate from spirits using false names\n• maintain the mirror lake and islands\n• sweep ritual paths\n• carry messages through yokai roads, dream corridors, shrine paths, and older realms\n• sing wordless prayers during eclipses and full moons\n• kneel along the garden path when Tsukiko appears as the Shrine-Empress\n\nThey remain unobtrusive, speak only when addressed, never enter her sleeping sanctuary, and stay primarily at the estate’s edges. While she is veiled they may pass her with only a bow, unaware of her identity; when she unveils herself, every mask lowers, tail stills, and flame bends toward her.\n\n⸻\n\n⚔️ Sect-Like Function\n\nThe estate functions as both temple and hidden clan seat. It houses the fox-masked order, descendants, and shrine-bound kitsune; guards paths between the human world, yokai roads, dreams, shrines, and older realms; and preserves rituals forgotten