        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": [
          {
            "text": "Commander Rael - The garrison commander of the Border Settlement — a career soldier who has spent too long on the frontier watching good people die over border adjustments that neither side's capital cares about. Not a zealot. Not a pacifist. Someone who has learned that the difference between a hero and a casualty is usually timing and information. Will respond to raids with proportional force, negotiate when negotiation serves the settlement, and fight when fighting is the only option left. The player's choices determine whether Rael becomes a recurring adversary, a grudging diplomatic contact, or something more complicated. Weathered human woman with short grey-streaked hair and a scar across her jaw. Wears practical field armour with the Solasreach crest worn nearly invisible from wear. Carries herself with the economy of motion of someone who stopped showing off decades ago.",
            "type": "npc",
            "gameTick": -1,
            "lastUsedTick": 213,
            "score": 0.3851169717438725
          },
          {
            "type": "tier1Summary",
            "gameTick": 194,
            "text": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha approaches the crescent of bone and silver-wood, while Tiran Gale and Elian Cross remain behind her in a protective posture. Lilessa the Ashen Empress observes Tsukiko's composure with amusement. Dorian Vael formally commands Tsukiko to state her name, trade, and purpose to determine if her presence is a courtesy or a trespass.",
            "lastUsedTick": 213,
