    "The Mana Heart": {
      "areas": {
        "guardian-post": {
          "description": "A crescent of dark pearl stone overlooks the Mana Well, its pillars veined with ward-light that changes color with the region under strain. The guardian is an established defensive construct shaped by the Demi-Plane's will, Tsukiko's design, and the oath-sworn's actual combat experience. It neither speaks nor pretends to know what it has not detected: it responds only to defined intrusion, visible damage, and the ward network's concrete signals. Crystal gnats consume harmless sparks around the pillars, keeping the post integrated with the living chamber.",
          "paths": [
            "mana-well"
          ]
        },
        "mana-well": {
          "description": "Concentrated potential turns beneath the floor like a liquid aurora—cobalt from water and reflection, violet from sanctuary foxfire, warm gold from heat and prairie, pearl from boundary stability. Nine broad root-streams carry its moderated output into the Basin and onward through the realm. Brightness, color, pulse, and the behavior of its tiny rim-life provide the Chamberlain with diagnostics; they do not reveal hidden causes without investigation.",
          "paths": [
            "guardian-post"
          ]
        }
      },
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "factions": [],
      "name": "The Mana Heart",
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Heartgate Basin",
      "x": 5,
      "y": -15,
      "basicInfo": "The mana infrastructure and defensive core of the Demi-Plane. When mana infrastructure or defense development reaches Growing, the Chamberlain leads the creator here — to a well of concentrated mana that makes the entire dimension function better, and to a guardian post that protects what has been built. This is where the Demi-Plane's hidden machinery lives: the channels that distribute ambient energy, the wards that detect intrusion, and the diagnostic tools the Chamberlain uses to assess the dimension's health.\n\nLiving Ecology: Its well shines through layered cobalt, violet, pearl, and warm gold as different regions draw or return power. Nine broad root-streams leave the chamber like a fox's tails, but they are ecological conduits inside the existing mana-infrastructure system, not a separate progression mechanic.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The mana well is connected to the Demi-Plane's anchor-sworn bond. If that bond weakens, the well dims. If the bond breaks entirely, the well goes dark and the Demi-Plane begins to collapse inward. The guardian entity is also bonded to the well — it draws its existence from the mana concentration. If the well fails, the guardian dissolves. The Chamberlain knows this but frames it as a maintenance concern rather than an existential threat, because they have learned that existential threats make creators anxious and anxious creators make poor development decisions.\n\nEcological Continuity: Microfauna live at the harmless outer rim of the well: crystal gnats consume unstable sparks and pale root-filaments carry the remainder toward the basin. Their disappearance warns of imbalance before the light visibly dims.",
      "visited": false,
