        "residential-row": {
          "description": "Small dwellings develop along a lantern-moss path as the Settlement system establishes them. Occupied homes reflect their actual occupants through furnishings and use; vacant homes stay simple, clean, and unclaimed rather than inventing hypothetical residents. Rain gardens between foundations keep water and animal routes connected to the wider Basin.",
