      "y": 5,
      "basicInfo": "The agricultural and residential heart of the Demi-Plane. When agriculture or settlement development reaches Growing, the Chamberlain leads the creator here — to soil that appeared from nothing and buildings that rose because someone needed shelter. This is where the Demi-Plane starts to feel like it could sustain life rather than merely contain it. Farm fields, a common hall, and residential quarters for oath-sworn residents.\n\nLiving Ecology: Between cultivated rows, low foxfire clover protects the soil, lantern moths pollinate by night, and narrow rills bring Dawn Stream water through living root filters. Its marked hall, fields, and residential row remain products of the established Agriculture and Settlement development stages; the richer ecology does not populate empty homes by itself.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Verdant Plot's soil is not ordinary earth. It is the Demi-Plane's latent potential made tangible — it grows what the creator and residents need most, not necessarily what they planted. A crop planted out of duty may produce something unexpected. A garden tended with genuine care produces abundantly. The Chamberlain has noticed this pattern but has not mentioned it. They are curious whether the creator will notice on their own.\n\nEcological Continuity: The soil answers actual need and sustained care through crop behavior rather than conjuring solutions without cost. Blue-veined leaves signal mana excess, pearl flowers signal thirst, and warm-gold fruit marks a stable balance between cultivation and the Basin's wider root network.",
