      "basicInfo": "A small roadside shrine dedicated to a minor goddess of travelers and safe passage — a stone altar, a carved wooden roof, and a tradition of leaving offerings for good luck on the road. The shrine is maintained by a solitary priestess who also sells minor blessing charms and restorative tea to passersby. She asks nothing, expects nothing, and somehow always has exactly what you need. Travelers who leave an offering report unusually good luck on the next leg of their journey.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The goddess is real, and the priestess is her mortal vessel. The goddess is too minor to intervene directly in world events, but she can tip the odds for travelers she likes — and she likes everyone who treats her shrine with respect.",
