      "basicInfo": "A misty depression in the western marsh where will-o-wisps gather in numbers found nowhere else in Aerfála. The Hollow is also home to a coven of marsh-witches who trade potions, curses, and information with anyone willing to pay their prices — which are never entirely in coin. The witches are not evil, but they are not nice either; they serve the marsh's ecology, and the marsh does not care about human morality. Visitors who treat the Hollow with respect leave with useful alchemical goods and occasionally a love potion that actually works. Visitors who do not respect the Hollow leave changed in ways they did not choose.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The coven's leader is a demon-blooded mage who chose the marsh over the Demon Lord's Army. She is genuinely committed to her coven. She is also genuinely dangerous when crossed. Her love potions work because she puts a piece of herself into every one.",
