    "Crossroads Academy": {
      "areas": {
        "courtyard": {
          "description": "The social heart of the Academy — a sprawling flagstone plaza between the Grand Hall, the Library, and the dormitories. Fountain-statues of the four founding races (human, elf, dwarf, beastkin) mark the cardinal directions. Students cluster on benches between classes, trading notes, gossip, and meaningful glances. The café cart by the south gate does a brisk trade in coffee and pastries from dawn to dusk.",
          "paths": [
            "grand-hall",
            "library",
            "martial-arena",
            "magic-tower",
            "male-dormitory",
            "female-dormitory",
            "faculty-wing",
            "gardens"
          ]
        },
        "faculty-wing": {
          "description": "The private offices and chambers of the Academy's instructors — a quieter wing with soundproofed doors and wards against eavesdropping. Office hours are posted; most students learn which professors keep them and which consider office hours a suggestion. The Headmistress's study sits at the end of the hall behind a door that is always locked and sometimes warm to the touch.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard"
          ]
        },
        "female-dormitory": {
          "description": "The women's residence hall — four floors of shared rooms, private study alcoves, and a basement laundry that is inexplicably the best place on campus for gossip. The ground-floor common room has a perpetually warm hearth, mismatched sofas, and an unspoken rule that what is said here stays here. The curfew bell rings at eleven. Nobody enforces it. Everyone pretends to obey it.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard",
            "gardens"
          ]
        },
        "gardens": {
          "description": "The Academy's cultivated wilderness — hedged walkways, flowering arches, a lotus pond, and enough secluded benches that the groundskeeper has given up mapping them. The eastern wall borders the Lowland meadows; the western wall has a gate that is technically locked at sunset. Moonlit visits to the gardens are a campus tradition that the faculty officially disapproves of and privately remembers fondly.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard",
            "female-dormitory",
            "male-dormitory"
          ]
        },
        "grand-hall": {
          "description": "The Academy's assembly chamber and dining hall — vaulted ceilings enchanted to show the sky outside, long tables for communal meals, and a raised dais for announcements, duels, and the occasional impromptu musical performance. Morning assemblies are mandatory. Afternoon assemblies are packed anyway because someone is always doing something worth watching.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard"
          ]
        },
        "library": {
          "description": "Three floors of towering shelves, restricted sections behind warded glass, and study carrels that students claim like territory. The head librarian is a reanimated sage who has been dead for four centuries and has no patience for noise. The restricted section requires faculty authorization — or sufficient cleverness to bypass a ward that has defeated at least six students per semester.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard"
          ]
        },
        "magic-tower": {
          "description": "The spellcasting wing — practice halls warded against miscast explosions, elemental labs that smell of ozone and brimstone, and the observation deck at the top where advanced students test long-range spells under supervision. The tower hums faintly at all hours from the residual mana of decades of practice. Accidental magical mishaps are the leading cause of wardrobe emergencies on campus.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard"
          ]
        },
        "male-dormitory": {
          "description": "The men's residence hall — four floors of shared rooms, a weight room in the basement that is never empty, and a rooftop access hatch that is technically forbidden and universally known. The ground-floor common room smells permanently of leather oil and ambition. The curfew bell is acknowledged the way speed limits are acknowledged on open roads.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard",
            "gardens"
          ]
        },
        "martial-arena": {
          "description": "The combat training complex — indoor sparring rings, an outdoor colosseum for ranked duels and tournament exhibitions, and the equipment vault where practice weapons are checked out and occasionally not returned. The sand is replaced monthly. The bloodstains are not. Ranked exhibition matches draw the whole campus; romantic tensions between duelists draw even more spectators.",
          "paths": [
            "courtyard"
          ]
        }
      },
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "factions": [],
      "name": "Crossroads Academy",
      "radius": 6,
      "region": "Bréanriv Lowlands",
      "x": 6.813351365237939,
      "y": -6.813351365237939,
      "basicInfo": "The continent's premier magic and martial academy — a sprawling hilltop campus in the Bréanriv Lowlands where the gifted, the noble, and the desperate converge to learn the arts of war and sorcery. Founded by a pact between the four great kingdoms after the Catastrophe, Crossroads Academy operates under international charter: no kingdom's soldiers may enter its grounds, no kingdom's laws supersede its internal governance. The Academy trains mages and warriors from every race and nation — though the demographics tilt heavily toward nobility with the coin to pay tuition and the connections to secure recommendation letters.\n\nScholarship students exist — roughly one in five attendees — and they are both envied and resented in equal measure. Scholarship requires either exceptional aptitude or a patron's sponsorship, and the Academy's aptitude tests are notoriously unforgiving. Those who earn their place by talent alone carry a quiet pride that old-money students find infuriating.\n\nThe campus runs on a rhythm of lectures, sparring sessions, practical exams, and the веч nocturnal drama of young adults living in close quarters with minimal supervision. Romances spark and fizzle. Rivalries escalate and cool. And somewhere in the faculty wing, someone is always watching for the students whose potential exceeds their rank.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Academy's neutrality is a polite fiction. The Demon Lord's intelligence network has placed at least two operatives among the faculty and several among the student body — demons and demonesses who have concealed their nature with transformation magic and enrolled to cultivate relationships with the nobility, gather strategic intelligence, and occasionally recruit talented students into contracts they will regret. The Headmistress is aware of at least one and has chosen not to act — because the information she extracts from the operative's presence is worth more than the risk. The other operative she does not know about is the more dangerous one.",
