      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "The Hearth Springs": {
      "areas": {
        "garden-path": {
          "description": "A winding path crosses steam-orchid beds, lantern ferns, warm stone, and quiet seats under miniature foxwood. Flowers drawn from real memories grow beside species invented by the Demi-Plane's own ecology, with violetwing moths carrying pollen through the vapor. The path becomes more elaborate through established Recreation development while preserving living root and water lanes.",
          "paths": [
            "hot-spring"
          ]
        },
        "hot-spring": {
          "description": "A sequence of clear pools rises from moonstone ledges without furnace or volcanic vent. Their mineral glow shifts from silver to violet to gold as the wider realm circulates, and steam curls into fleeting tail-shapes before returning as dew. Bathing eases fatigue and improves recovery through gentle mana conversion; it does not suppress emotion, erase injury, or force relaxation.",
          "paths": [
            "garden-path",
            "trade-post"
          ]
        },
        "trade-post": {
          "description": "A covered exchange and workshop court beside the springs, fitted with secure storage, craft benches, a ledger station, and a receiving line from the Anchor. Its pale counters are inlaid with fallen spirit wood and shell crystal. The facility supports actual commerce when access, goods, and traders are established; it never generates merchants, inventory, or sales by itself.",
          "paths": [
            "hot-spring"
          ]
        }
      },
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "factions": [],
      "name": "The Hearth Springs",
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Heartgate Basin",
      "x": -10,
      "y": 15,
      "basicInfo": "The recreational and commercial district of the Demi-Plane. When recreation or commerce development reaches Growing, the Chamberlain leads the creator here — to hot springs that bubbled up from nothing, gardens that grew because someone wished for beauty, and a trade post ready for the first merchant willing to do business with a pocket dimension. This is where the Demi-Plane starts to feel worth visiting, not just worth building.\n\nLiving Ecology: The pools lie in a garden of steam-orchids, moonstone ledges, and moss that glows only through vapor. Each spring takes on a faint regional color as the Demi-Plane circulates—silver after northern thaw, violet after Mirror Mere, and gold after Southroll pollen season—making the district feel native to Tsukiko's realm rather than an Aerfálan bathhouse copied into it.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The hot spring's water has a subtle restorative effect — not healing, but rejuvenating. Visitors who bathe here recover from fatigue faster and find their mood improved. The Chamberlain attributes this to the Demi-Plane responding to the creator's needs. In truth, the spring is drawing on the ambient mana that the Demi-Plane's infrastructure channels, converting it into a form that benefits living things. If mana infrastructure ever fails, the spring's effects diminish.\n\nEcological Continuity: Steam moths feed on mineral vapor and carry spring-orchid pollen along the garden path. Their wing color provides the earliest sign that the water's restorative conversion is weakening.",
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": [],
      "known": true
    },
    "The Howling Hollow": {
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
