    "The Raiding Grounds": {
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "factions": [
        "Demon Lord's Army"
      ],
      "name": "The Raiding Grounds",
      "radius": 5,
      "region": "Demon Realm",
      "x": 28.893755415948608,
      "y": 21.106244584051392,
      "basicInfo": "The mortal-side territory adjacent to the Borderlands — frontier settlements, supply roads, minor noble estates, and the occasional dungeon-adjacent town that has grown up around an adventurer economy. This is where excursions operate. Raids are not random. Experienced demon commanders identify targets by resource value, defensive weakness, proximity to mortal military response, and political consequence. What raids bring back: food and material resources, gold, weapons and armour, intelligence on mortal military dispositions, and occasionally people — captives whose presence in the fief creates its own narrative weight. The narrator handles captive NPCs as full characters with their own perspective on their situation. Captivity is never romanticized. While a person is a captive — held, owned, indebted, or bound in any way — they are not available as a romantic option, and the narrator must not write romance with them under any circumstances. There are no exceptions for mutual attraction, reciprocity, or player initiative; a captive cannot freely consent to a captor, and the narrator does not pretend otherwise. The only trajectory the narrator advances with a captive is toward their freedom. Romance becomes possible only if and after the captive has been genuinely freed — released from every hold, debt, obligation, or claim over them — and, standing as a true equal with the full ability to walk away, chooses the player of their own independent will. Any attraction that exists before that point is subordinate to the captive's autonomy and their right to leave; the narrator resolves such situations by moving toward liberation, never toward romance.",
      "hiddenInfo": "A mortal intelligence network operates in the Raiding Grounds — scouts and informants who report demon movements to the frontier garrison. The network has been penetrated by a demon agent who feeds selective information to the fief. Neither side fully trusts their own intelligence.",
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "The Verdant Archive": {
