    "The Hidden Estate of the Mother Fox": {
      "name": "The Hidden Estate of the Mother Fox",
      "basicInfo": "The ancestral seat of Tsukiko Kuzunoha, the primordial Mother of All Kitsune, hidden within her sacred Veiled Fox Sanctuary. Behind high warm-clay walls under black tiles and a crimson-lacquered gate, cherry blossoms and illusion conceal a compound that combines Heian Shinden-zukuri aristocracy with the spiritual gravity of a Tendai temple. Outsiders perceive a forgotten ruined temple swallowed by forest; permitted guests enter a serene, disciplined estate reached only through the sanctuary itself, never from the wider Demi-Plane. Tsukiko keeps no casual jewelry and favors soft inner robes, layered Heian silk, and seasonal kasane colors; her private rooms smell of hinoki, toasted rice tea, sakura, incense, clean skin, and foxfire. The estate is both home and hidden clan seat of the fox-masked Kitsune no Kage: shrine-bound kitsune, distant descendants, orphaned fox spirits, yokai retainers, household spirits, and lesser kitsune drawn to the Mother Flame through blood or spirit, serving from devotion and instinctive recognition rather than wages. The compound includes the sutra-engraved Mon, central Shinden pavilion, sealed Kita-no-in, eastern kōdō and calligraphy hall, guest wing, moonlit transformation dojo, and a sacred spirit garden centered on a crescent mirror lake. The estate is elegant, private, quietly populated, and fully alive beneath its apparent stillness.\n\nLiving Ecology: The crescent lake, old garden pines, foxfire lanterns, and sanctuary woodland form a closed living circuit around the compound. Lantern koi consume excess foxfire, violet moss filters roofwater, and fallen cherry petals become luminous soil beneath the outer groves, making the estate feel grown into Tsukiko's realm rather than placed upon it.",
