      "x": -6,
      "y": -6,
      "areas": {
        "front-gate": {
          "description": "The Mon — a massive gabled red-lacquer gate engraved with an ancient Tendai sutra and a discreet fox crest, opening only when Tsukiko summons it. It stands beneath the high warm-clay perimeter walls, whose roofline conceals an invisible guardian inscription legible only to yokai. Beyond the gate: the estate-court on raked white gravel, foxfire lantern posts along moss-grown stone terraces, and paths toward the spirit-garden.",
          "paths": [
            "estate-court"
          ]
        },
        "central-pavilion": {
          "description": "The Shinden — an elevated open hall with long verandas and an open-sky inner courtyard. Screens painted with golden mist and ink-brushed foxes divide meditation spaces, a hall for receiving gods, walking galleries, and chambers for tending spirit-wounded guests. Paper walls shift subtly for Tsukiko but remain rigid for others; corridors whisper to trusted people walking alone.",
          "paths": [
