        },
        "minami-no-in": {
          "description": "The moonlit silent southern dojo — polished dark wood open to the night, used for movement, balance, and transformation rather than combat. Foxfire lamps burn at exactly the brightness Tsukiko's mood sets.",
          "paths": [
            "central-pavilion"
          ]
        },
        "spirit-garden": {
          "description": "Behind the central hall: a slow crescent-shaped mirror lake with twin red bridges, supernatural koi, and floating foxfire. Its islands symbolize celestial tails — one holds a stone lantern said to contain the soul of the first fox born of Tsukiko's divine breath; another, wreathed in wisteria and moss, is her refuge when she wants solitude even from gods. Her reflection appears in the lake only when she permits it. Stone foxes in red bibs watch from mossy pedestals; paths cross in shimenawa-bound silence.",
