      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Skywatch Rise": {
      "name": "Skywatch Rise",
      "basicInfo": "The only rise in The Open Horizon — a low, broad swelling of ground a few meters higher than the plain around it. From its crest, the savanna unrolls to the glowing horizon in every direction, and the enormous sky feels larger still. Wild grass parts around its base as if in deference. At dusk the mana birds roost on its slopes, and their faint glow makes the rise look briefly like a low hill of embers.\n\nLiving Ecology: The Rise lifts only a few body-lengths above the savanna, yet its crown sits between the upper stars and their dew-bright twins below. Migrating sky rays circle it once before choosing their next current.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 10,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Open Horizon",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The rise was not there when the region formed — it swelled up on its own some days after, as if the plain wanted one vantage point from which to see itself. Grass does not grow on its crest; the ground there is smooth and slightly warm, and sitting on it makes intention unusually clear. Whoever sits at the crest and looks at the horizon with a single fixed purpose may find the plain quietly rearranging itself to match.\n\nEcological Continuity: Changes in herd routes and windseed drift can be read from here, but they remain observable evidence rather than supernatural certainty. The Rise offers perspective, not omniscience.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Open Horizon Plain": {
      "name": "Open Horizon Plain",
      "basicInfo": "The great open ground of The Open Horizon — kilometers of flat savanna beneath an enormous sky, unbroken except by Skywatch Rise. The horizon line glows faintly warm in every direction, like embers at the world's edge. Walking it is an experience of scale: sound carries forever, weather is visible an hour off, and footprints fade slowly into the humming grass.\n\nLiving Ecology: Horizon grass carries alternating silver and gold waves as the Demi-Plane's daily current reverses. Glasswing locust husks glitter along migration lanes, while open-ground foxes leave mirage trails that dissolve by noon.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "The Open Horizon",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The plain carries little fixed geographical bias, but its roots, water, winds, and migration lanes are already real. Clear development intent can shape it only through the established Expansion system, actual investment, and persistent consequences. Herds reroute before a viable change settles, while vague wishes produce no finished structure, free resources, or automatic result.\n\nEcological Continuity: The plain remains available to established expansion mechanics, but it is not ecologically blank. Development redirects roots, water, wind, and herds, and those consequences persist instead of vanishing once construction completes.",
