    "Mana-Density Survey Point": {
      "name": "Mana-Density Survey Point",
      "basicInfo": "A single pale stone standing in the tall grass of The Deep Expanse, ringed by a worn circle where the Chamberlain measures the region's mana density by hand — one of the earliest man-made places in the dimension. The stone is ordinary except that grass refuses to grow within its ring. A small notebook-sized hollow in the stone's base holds the latest readings, chalked in the Chamberlain's precise hand.\n\nLiving Ecology: Amber fungus appears in a wider ring after every healthy herd migration and shrinks when mana accumulates without biological use. The Chamberlain now records both phenomena beside the original readings.",
