      "radius": 1,
      "region": "The Deep Expanse",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The readings matter more than the region admits: the Expanse's mana density has crept steadily upward since measurement began, as if the reservoir below the prairie is filling faster than the dimension can spend it. A day is coming when the grass will hum loud enough to hear from the Stone Rise. Mana amber forms thickest within a hundred paces of the point. The Chamberlain has never explained the survey to the creator; he treats it as his private promise that the ground will be ready when she is.\n\nEcological Continuity: The rising reserve is safest when roots, herds, predators, and decomposers remain active. A high number alone does not mean unlimited power or automatic readiness for every project.",
