      "region": "The Southroll",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The Walk's path was never laid or trodden into being; it appeared complete the morning after the Southroll stabilized — the only fully finished feature the dimension ever produced unasked. Walking its full length in a single stretch grants mild, harmless euphoria and (the Chamberlain suspects) slightly improved mana sensitivity. Small spirit dens thread the embankments under the path: grass spirits and foxes share them without tension. Springs surface along the route after heavy warm days, occasionally ringing with firefly dust in the water.\n\nEcological Continuity: The firefly pattern is a response to airflow and body heat, not a message or judgment. Deviations can reveal ecological disturbance without supplying its cause automatically.",
