    "Eastern Clefts": {
      "name": "Eastern Clefts",
      "basicInfo": "The great fissure system of The Rift March — dark stone gorges twisting into the region's east, deep enough that cold blue light seeps upward from their bottoms at night. The rims echo a heartbeat late. Grassland edges carelessly into stone; the West is the Southroll's warmth, the East is depth, shadow, and something that has not decided whether it is scenery or danger. Cave mouths punctuate the cleft walls — most unplumbed, all unmarked.\n\nLiving Ecology: Cold-light fungus paints the deepest walls cobalt while darkroot vines bridge narrow gaps for crawlers and seed. Echo bats make the caverns audible in delayed, layered clicks.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 25,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "The Rift March",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The clefts descend toward the dimensional boundary itself; at a certain depth, visitors feel they are standing at the bottom of the world. Rift crawlers and cave drakes nest in the upper systems, but the deep systems hold unexplored caverns, monster nests of higher-level predators, and ruins of strange geometry that predate the March — materialized fears wear borrowed shapes. At least one fissure mouth reads as a natural dungeon entrance waiting for an occupant. Blue mana ore veins run along the deepest exposed walls, harvested only by the brave or the careless.\n\nEcological Continuity: The caves support dangerous fauna and future dungeon development but no unestablished culture, population, or ancient empire. Ruins appear only where existing canon or later play gives them a concrete origin.",
