    "Rift Overlook": {
      "name": "Rift Overlook",
      "basicInfo": "The grassland rim above the Eastern Clefts — a broad stone knoll where the Rift March's last safe ground meets its first true drop. From the overlook, the whole fissure system is visible: layered ridges sculpting downward into blue-lit dark. Wind rises from below at dusk carrying cold mineral air and, occasionally, a sound not quite echo. A low cairn ring marks the safety line; past it the ground breaks without warning.\n\nLiving Ecology: Golden Southroll grass ends in a clean dark rim overlooking the first blue-lit fissures. Cleft foxes den among warm western stones, safely above the rift crawlers' vertical routes.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 15,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Rift March",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The Chamberlain placed the cairn ring himself after two survey trips, but refuses to survey further without an escort — unusual fear for a being that catalogs monsters without hesitation. Blue-flame wisps rise from the clefts to the overlook on windless nights, circling it twice before sinking back: a behavior he logs but cannot explain. From this point, only the uppermost cave mouths are in sight; the true depths begin where the overlook's map ends and every route beyond is discovery, not documentation.\n\nEcological Continuity: The Overlook offers observable signs—roost flights, fungal brightness, echo delay—rather than automatic knowledge of what lives in unexplored depths.",
