    "Stillwater Shore": {
      "name": "Stillwater Shore",
      "basicInfo": "The formal coast of The Quiet Shore — the tideline where moon-white sand meets the flat, still air that behaves like unbreathing water. No waves arrive; sound does not travel. Glass crabs drift across the horizon as if skating, and the luminous fish-like entities glide deep beneath the surface of the not-water near the boundary, too far and too strange for study. The most peaceful and solitary place in the Demi-Plane.\n\nLiving Ecology: At false midnight the boundary dew gathers into perfect beads, rolls uphill through moon-sand, and disappears into shell beds that feed the western marshes. Glass crabs comb the tideline in silent, parallel rows.",
      "x": 15,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "The Quiet Shore",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The not-water is the region's unanswered question — the dimension's only undecided coastline. Walking into it presses no resistance; visitors walk back damp in spirit rather than body, as if the not-water touched what they are made of. Objects arrive on this shore with no origin: sealed bottles with no letters, ropes of no ships, lamps of no wreck. The Chamberlain records each, troubled only by his inability to find their source. The pale shore spirits gather on the tide-line at true dusk and face the horizon — the closest thing this dimension has to a ritual no one designed.\n\nEcological Continuity: The fish-shaped lights beneath the not-water are native boundary grazers following currents of reflected mana. They are living creatures, not trapped souls, omens, or inhabitants of an unseen city.",
