    },
    "Future Market Square": {
      "name": "Future Market Square",
      "basicInfo": "A flat, cleared rise in the western Westreach staked out with survey cordons and wooden pins — the Chamberlain's first choice for a market square. The ground here is unusually firm and level, roads in imagination already bend toward it from three directions, and the young treants have kept a respectful distance. Cowslip grows thick around the stakes as if decorating the future on the dimension's behalf.\n\nLiving Ecology: The measured rise remains alive with cowslip, dawn moths, and a root-safe ring of lantern saplings. Survey cords glow faintly wherever a future foundation can settle without blocking drainage or animal paths.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 30,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Westreach",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The soil here is the most construction-responsive in the Demi-Plane — foundations settle within days instead of weeks. A small well has already surfaced at the square's northeast corner, unmarked and unfinished, apparently the dimension getting a head start. The Chamberlain visits weekly to log ground changes; he has sketched a full market design but refuses to break ground without the creator's word. Objects pinned under the cordon stakes overnight tend to be exactly what the future market's first traders will need.\n\nEcological Continuity: The site supports the existing Commerce development path but does not summon traders, stock, customers, or buildings. Those require actual access, construction, relationships, and exchange.",
