    "Guesthouse Site": {
      "name": "Guesthouse Site",
      "basicInfo": "A gentle south-facing slope in the central Westreach, staked as the future guesthouse grounds — level ground, good drainage, young trees saved for shade rather than cleared. The first visitors to the dimension will sleep here. A firepit ring has already appeared at the slope's foot, stones laid neatly by no visible hand.\n\nLiving Ecology: Foxfire dew beads thickly on the saved shade trees, and dewback tortoises use the slope as a dawn crossing. The spontaneous firepit sits above a natural dry-stone heat seam rather than ordinary copied campcraft.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 45,
