    "Training Yard Site": {
      "name": "Training Yard Site",
      "basicInfo": "A broad, hard-packed flat in the eastern Westreach closest to the core, staked as the future training yard — the flattest, firmest ground in the region, deliberately kept clear of even sapling trees. The soil compacts underfoot like packed earth of a much older settlement. Face-worn distances make someone standing at one end feel the other end is nearer than it looks: not quite right, but not quite wrong either.\n\nLiving Ecology: The compacted ground sheds rain toward a border of shock-absorbing violet moss. Jewel beetles gather harmless residual mana after strenuous movement, keeping repeated practice from scorching the soil.",
      "x": 12,
      "y": 38,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Westreach",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The hard ground is the dimension's doing — the region foresaw combat practice and pre-compacted the soil. Nothing here grows, and footsteps sound of old ground in a young dimension. The slight spatial distortion is probably the mana channel's flow beneath it, making it ideal ground for training perception as well as the body. The Chamberlain keeps this site cleared personally and hopes the creator's oath-sworn residents will one day sweat here.\n\nEcological Continuity: Its slight spatial compression sharpens distance judgment but does not improve skills, award experience, or force training outcomes on its own. Mechanical advancement remains governed by the established systems.",
