    "Dawn Stream": {
      "name": "Dawn Stream",
      "basicInfo": "The young river of The Dawn Barrow — clear water that appeared without instruction, threading the meadow's open ground between wildflower clusters and wet-grass flats. Where it passes over red stone it glows faintly, as if the water and the stone are pleased to meet. The stream feels newly made in the best sense: every bend is a place the dimension noticed and improved, and objects keep arriving in its current from regions far away.\n\nLiving Ecology: Ribbonfin flash beneath flower islands, mist swallows skim insects from the bends, and the current changes from silver to violet to gold according to what the upstream regions have recently released.",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "The Dawn Barrow",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The stream flows out of the Mirror Mere — the dimension's first autonomous connection between its own regions, hydrology designed by no one. It is still growing a personality: some bends pocket a slow warm pool, others sharpen overnight into small waterfalls, and at least one stretch runs over an undercut cave that the water made for hiding. Flower islands — mats of wetland blooms riding slow currents — migrate downstream on windless days. The Chamberlain logs each change with more optimism than any other entry in his ledgers.\n\nEcological Continuity: The colors record carried material and mana state only. They do not reveal who caused a change, what anyone intended, or unseen events without evidence reaching the water.",
