    },
    "Bamboo Spring": {
      "name": "Bamboo Spring",
      "basicInfo": "A spring of clear water pooling beneath sweeping bamboo at the edge of the sanctuary's inner groves — the quietest water in the dimension. The bamboo grows in deliberate rows, pale and faintly luminous; the spring surface holds reflection without ripple. Tea water drawn here never cools as quickly as it should, and foxfire blooms cluster at the bank as if keeping watch.\n\nLiving Ecology: Overflow from the spring slips beneath the bamboo in three clear threads: one feeds the sanctuary grove, one becomes Meadow dew, and one sinks toward the Quiet Shore's buried shell beds. Lantern koi and translucent spring-snails keep the basin clear without attendants needing to manage a decorative pond.",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 45,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "Veiled Fox Sanctuary",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The spring is fed through the shinboku's root system, which is why its water carries a faint sense of Tsukiko's calm — drinking it settles intention and quiets fear. Sacred bamboo harvested here is the strongest conduit-wood in the Demi-Plane for wardwork and writing. A low stone basin sits half-buried at the bank, older in style than everything around it; moss rarely touches it, and the estate staff refill it weekly as if it were furniture. On some mornings the spring's reflection briefly contains a vermilion gate that is not standing anywhere nearby.\n\nEcological Continuity: The water settles fear because it dampens magical turbulence, not because it changes choices or feelings. Its effect is brief, gentle, and never overrides player agency, personality, or memory.",
