    },
    "Fox Statues": {
      "name": "Fox Statues",
      "basicInfo": "The paired stone foxes seated on either side of the Beginning's Torii — guardian kami in the household style, mossy-pedestaled and bibbed, gazing calmly outward from the crossing. They are the First Meadow's only permanent fixtures, and the meadow's growth respects them, keeping the grass trimmed around their bases in neat circles.\n\nLiving Ecology: Duskbees shelter beneath the stone paws during rain, and foxfire clover grows in nine small arcs around each pedestal. Their red bibs draw no dirt even when warm pollen falls thickly.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 25,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "The First Meadow",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The statues are not merely decoration — they are the sanctuary's outermost watchers and part of its ward-line. Offerings left at their feet (flowers, herbs, one coin once) vanish by the following dawn; sprigs of foxfire bloom appear in return. The left fox faces outward toward the meadow and the right fox faces inward toward the sanctuary, and at dusk each turns its head a fraction to follow the other's gaze. The Chamberlain has observed this for a season and decided it falls politely under the category of things he does not need to understand.\n\nEcological Continuity: Offerings disappear because the ward-root absorbs compatible material and returns it as foxfire bloom. The statues do not grant wishes, assign quests, or communicate unknown information without an established effect.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
