    },
    "Northern Approach": {
      "name": "Northern Approach",
      "basicInfo": "The formal opening of The Threshold March toward the North Field — a stretch of cleared, firmed ground where the corridor's paths gather and run north together. The ground here feels expectant, as if widened by the dimension in anticipation of future traffic. Low stone markers the Chamberlain placed line the route; the reed-seeds drift thickest here at dusk, strung out like slow lanterns over the road north.\n\nLiving Ecology: Lantern cranes rest beside the marker stones, reed voles tunnel beneath the verges, and every moving seed aligns north when the Field's channels are about to surface nearby.",
      "x": 15,
      "y": 45,
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "The Threshold March",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The ground firms where repeated permitted travel actually occurs, and the Chamberlain's marker stones measure how far the corridor's mana channel has extended north. Reed alignment, tracks, and compressed grass record concrete passage only. The Approach does not generate abandoned camps, merchants, travelers, or visitors; every non-native arrival still requires the established Gate or Anchor access.",
