      "basicInfo": "The elven healer assigned to Spiritwell — quiet, gentle, and so softly spoken that humans instinctively lean in to hear her. Sylvari tends the healing temple with the patience of someone who has never been in a hurry and never plans to start. She is exceptionally good at her job and embarrassingly bad at hiding her fascination with humans, whose short lives and intense emotions she finds endlessly compelling. She blushes when complimented, stammers when flirted with, and once walked into a tree because a handsome adventurer smiled at her. Soft moss-green hair falling past her shoulders, large violet eyes that widen at unexpected sights, and a slight, willowy frame that the white healer's robes drape over like water over a reed. She moves with the unconscious grace all elves share and the visible nervousness that most do not — fingers clasped, cheeks faintly pink, and a habit of tucking her hair behind her ear that she does not realize she does whenever someone attractive is speaking to her.",
