      "basicInfo": "A wandering Seeker scholar who has been camped at the edge of the Palebark Ruins for the past three years, mapping the architecture and cataloguing the residual enchantments. Tarn is in his fifties, perpetually rumpled, and the most cheerful person in the ruins by a wide margin — possibly the only cheerful person within ten miles. He buys drinks for anyone who brings him news from the outside world and pays in stories about the ruins that scholars elsewhere would consider career-defining. Middle-aged, brown-and-grey hair in a thinning ponytail, beard kept short for practical rather than aesthetic reasons. He wears layered scholar's robes patched at the elbows and travel boots that have been resoled three times. His eyes are bright with constant intellectual delight. His hands are stained with ink and the faint silver residue of pre-Collapse glyph-touching.",
