      "basicInfo": "The Academy's Chief Combat Instructor — a half-dwarf built like a barrel and twice as hard to tip over. Marshal Stonehand teaches the martial curriculum from E-rank fundamentals through B-rank advanced techniques, and he has never once gone easy on a student regardless of their bloodline. His sparring sessions are the most feared hours on any student's schedule.\n\nGarret retired from active adventuring at B-rank after twenty years in the field — not because he could not go further, but because he decided he preferred making sure the next generation survived long enough to surpass him. He has trained three A-rank fighters, one S-rank candidate, and more B-ranks than he can count. His former students send him letters. He pretends to find this annoying. Broad as a doorframe, thick-armed, and moving with the deliberate economy of someone who has learned that wasted motion means wasted years. Brown skin, close-cropped iron-grey hair, and a jaw that looks like it was carved from the same stone he teaches students to break. His right hand occasionally shakes; he keeps it in his pocket or on a weapon grip. He wears reinforced instructor's leathers that have seen actual combat, and his voice carries across the arena without effort. Students have nightmares about that voice saying 'again.'",
