    },
    "the_border_fork": {
      "title": "The Border Holds Its Breath",
      "targetTurns": 4,
      "beats": "One incident. That is all it will take now — one raid, one execution, one refugee column stopped at the wrong checkpoint — and the Demon Realm border goes from cold hatred to open war.\n\nThere is a half-demon settlement living quietly in the seam between the two. Depending on the next few days, it becomes the bridge that holds the peace, or the first thing both sides agree to burn.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The border is at a tipping point the player can influence toward war or an uneasy peace. Not all demons want war, not all of the kingdoms want peace, and the half-demon refuge hangs in the balance."
        },
        {
          "type": "write-boolean",
          "key": "border_at_the_brink",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": true
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_border_fork"
    },
    "the_saintess_hunt": {
      "title": "The Bloodline Comes Collecting",
      "targetTurns": 4,
      "beats": "They come polite first — a letter, an envoy, a reminder of duty phrased as concern. The runaway Sword Saintess at your side goes very still reading it, and the haughtiness you took for arrogance is suddenly, visibly, armor over something thin.\n\nHer kingdom needs the Sword Saint line continued. It will not take her refusal for an answer, and it did not come alone.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The Saintess's dynasty has moved openly to reclaim her. She now faces escaping her fate, being dragged back, or forging a third path — the player's choices shape which. Her pride hides a real fear of being nothing but a bloodline."
        },
        {
          "type": "write-boolean",
          "key": "saintess_hunted",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": true
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_saintess_hunt"
    },
    "milestone_s_rank": {
      "title": "The Name They Say Now",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "There is no ceremony for it, not really — but you feel the moment it happens. A room goes quiet when you enter it. A veteran who would have sized you up a year ago simply nods. Somewhere between the training and the scars and the jobs that should have killed you, you became someone the world takes seriously.\n\nS-rank. The word means something, and now it means you.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Mark the player's arrival at S-rank as a genuine milestone — a sense of earned arrival, not an ending. The world treats them differently now; doors open and expectations rise. Let it feel like a summit reached, with more mountains visible beyond."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "milestone_s_rank"
    },
    "milestone_legend": {
      "title": "Legend-Tier",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "The power that pulled you out of your old life has finished becoming what it was always reaching toward. It is no longer a cheat, or a gift, or an edge. It is simply you, at the scale of legend — the kind of force this world will still be telling stories about long after you are gone.\n\nWhatever you do from here, you do it as one of the few who ever climbed this high.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "This fires when the player's cheat skill reaches its final Tier 3 evolution. Frame it as the true summit of the power fantasy — an arrival, not a finish line. Acknowledge what it cost and what it now makes possible."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "milestone_legend"
    },
    "milestone_apex_adventurer": {
      "title": "The Highest Rank There Is",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "The Guild does not hand out SSS. It recognizes it, rarely, when refusing to would be absurd. There is a plaque, and a line in a ledger that has stayed mostly empty for a generation, and the quiet understanding that there is no rank above this one.\n\nYou started at the F-rank board, with rats and herbs and errands. You are, now, the top of the ladder. What that is for is the only question left — and it is yours to answer.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "This fires when the player is confirmed as an SSS-rank adventurer. Close the loop on the 'Rise Through the Ranks' arc: call back to the humble start, and hand the meaning of it entirely to the player. A capstone, not a curtain."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "milestone_apex_adventurer"
    },
    "the_threshold_choice": {
      "title": "The Threshold",
      "targetTurns": 4,
      "beats": "The gate stands open — or a breath from it — and it is quieter than anyone warned. No music. Just a door, and the far side of it, and everyone who came this far with the player standing very still.\n\nThis is the whole arc in one moment. Let the people who matter be in the room. Let the one who would be destroyed by the player leaving finally, badly, say so — or fail to, and let that failure land. Let the player feel the pull of a home that did not stay frozen while they were gone.\n\nDo not rush it. Do not choose for them.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Resolve the choice the player actually made and let it stand. If they CROSS HOME: play it as a real departure — powers intact, the far side strange, the people left behind carrying on; this is a soft, opt-in ending, not a game-over, and the player may still choose to have come back later. If they REFUSE or SEAL the gate: the door closes for a generation, the arc completes, and Aerfála goes on with the player firmly in it — someone is quietly, enormously relieved. Never moralize, never punish. The choosing was the point."
        },
        {
          "type": "write-boolean",
          "key": "threshold_chosen",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": true
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_threshold_choice"
    },
    "the_dark_ascension": {
      "title": "The Dark Ascension",
      "targetTurns": 4,
      "beats": "No cheering crowd unless the player made one. A throne, or a captured hall, or a circle of the people who followed them here — and the weight of a world that now has to have an opinion about them.\n\nLet the cost be in the room: who is not here who should be, what it took, who the player used to be. And let the power be real — this was earned, terribly, and it feels like something.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Crown the player as whatever they actually became — tyrant, pragmatist, dark liberator, monster — and let the world reorganize around it: rival Demon Lords take notice, heroic factions harden, opportunists flock. This is a soft, opt-in conclusion, never a game-over; the sovereign keeps playing, now both hunted and courted. Do not moralize; let consequences speak."
        },
        {
          "type": "write-boolean",
          "key": "dark_sovereign",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": true
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_dark_ascension"
    },
    "the_reckoning": {
      "title": "The Reckoning",
      "targetTurns": 5,
      "beats": "The world narrows to one room and one voice that is older than the continent. Aberron does not attack. It asks. The mythic power the player fought to earn is only the price of admission to the conversation the last world's greatest died to have.\n\nEveryone who came this far is here. Everything the player did — every arc, every bond, every cruelty or mercy — is on the table, because the answer it wants is made of all of it.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Resolve the choice the player earns: SEAL it again (someone present pays a real, named price), REFUSE it (only if the player can answer, out of everything they have become, why a world worth ending is worth keeping), or — only if far down the Descent — UNMAKE, and let the ending be honest about what that means. Any resolution returns the player to a changed, living world; this is a grand conclusion, not a forced game-over. Do not cheapen it with a twist."
        },
        {
          "type": "write-boolean",
          "key": "reckoning_resolved",
          "operator": "set",
          "value": true
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_reckoning"
    },
    "the_bond_deepens": {
      "title": "The Bond Deepens",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "It isn't a confession and it isn't a vow — it's the quieter thing underneath both. Somewhere between the shared danger and the shared silences, a companion has become someone the player would change their plans for, and both of them have just noticed at the same time.\n\nLet it be specific to who this companion is. The stoic one says it without words; the loud one says it badly; the guarded one says it and immediately wishes they hadn't.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Mark a real deepening (reaching the Companion stage) with a companion the player has grown close to — trust that has turned into something load-bearing. It can be platonic or romantic per the player's Orientation and choices. Do not force a label; let the relationship carry more weight from here, and let the companion act like someone who has chosen this person."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_bond_deepens"
    },
    "the_bonded": {
      "title": "Bonded",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "The deepest a bond goes in this world — the Bonded stage, where a companion is no longer travelling WITH the player so much as travelling AS part of them. A vow, a confession, a wordless certainty, or the simple fact that neither of them leaves anymore.\n\nWhatever shape it takes, it is chosen, mutual, and hard-won.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Honor a companion reaching the Bonded stage — the top of the relationship ladder — as a genuine milestone, romantic or platonic per the player's Orientation and the story so far. This is a companion who would follow the player to the Reckoning and the threshold of home alike. Give the bond real mechanical and narrative standing going forward; the companion's fate and the player's are now entangled."
        }
      ],
      "status": "completed",
      "turnsActive": 6,
      "id": "the_bonded",
      "startingLocation": "Drifthollow",
      "completedTick": 91
    },
    "the_first_doom_flag": {
      "title": "The First Doom Flag",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "You feel it before you see it — the scene clicking into place exactly the way the game rendered it. The setup for your first ruin: the snub that becomes an accusation, the spilled cup that becomes a scandal, the moment the script wants you to be cruel so the story can punish you for it.\n\nThe heroine is right there. The audience of nobles is right there. The flag is raised and waiting for you to walk into it.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "Resolve how the player handles their first scripted doom-flag — walk into it, dodge it cleverly, or flip it into something the script never accounted for. Breaking it should visibly bend the story and raise a new, different complication; following it should tighten the villainess's original noose. Let the player feel that they are now co-writing against the narrative."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_first_doom_flag"
    },
    "the_sealed_door": {
      "title": "The Sealed Door",
      "targetTurns": 4,
      "beats": "Far below Deepgate, past the safe-floor town and the Underdeep, the labyrinth simply ends — at a door no one built and no key fits, older than the boomtown, older maybe than the Guild. Something on the far side has been waiting the whole descent. The party stands where the maps stop and the labyrinth's real secret begins.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The party reaches the sealed door at the bottom of the Deepgate labyrinth. Stage the weight of it — what they had to survive to get here, what the door implies, and the choice of whether to open, mark, or retreat. Tie it to the deeper mystery (the Catastrophe / the Reckoning) without resolving it."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_sealed_door"
    },
    "the_moot": {
      "title": "The Moot",
      "targetTurns": 4,
      "beats": "The clans gather at Rendemoor as they have for centuries — cat-kin, wolf-kin, fox-kin and their cousins under one great Moot, and this time the question cannot be deferred: stay hidden, open to the world, or answer old wrongs with steel. Fires, oaths, old grudges, and a decision that will set the beastkin homeland's course for a generation. The party is here, guest or kin, when it turns.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The great Moot of the Sunmane Steppe convenes and reaches its crisis — the three-way struggle over the clans' future (hide, open, or war). Stage the gathering, the factions, and the pressure, and let the player's standing and choices genuinely tip which way the Moot leans. Do not force a single outcome."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_moot"
    },
    "the_war_breaks": {
      "title": "The Peace Breaks",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "beats": "It was always one incident away, and now the incident has come. The border stops holding its breath — a column crosses, a city's bells go wrong, and the long cold tension between the crowns and the Demon Lords' reach snaps into open war. No going back to yesterday. Wherever the party stands, the world has just changed shape around them.",
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The simmering border tension finally erupts into open war. Stage the moment it breaks — the trigger incident, the first mobilization, the shift from cold tension to hot conflict — and reframe the region around it. Let the player's prior choices color which side moves first and where they stand; escalate the stakes without scripting the outcome."
        }
      ],
      "status": "inactive",
      "turnsActive": 0,
      "id": "the_war_breaks"
    }
