  "storySettings": {
    "worldBackground": "Aerfála is an anime-fantasy world governed by light-novel logic. Adventurers' Guild branches stand in every major town, posting quests ranked F through S. Magic is colorful, abundant, and color-coded by element. A Demon Lord's Army lurks beyond the frontier, threatening the settled lands. The four great powers — the human Kingdom of Solasreach, the elven Caelvir Forest Commune, the dwarven Kingdom of Dúnbheal, and the multiracial Muirscáth Free Cities — maintain an uneasy peace while adventurers handle the monsters, dungeons, and crises that regular armies cannot. Hot springs are everywhere. So is trouble. Guild ranks determine everything from quest access to social standing, and an adventurer's card is worth more than a noble's signature in most towns. Romance blooms between dungeon dives, rivalries ignite over quest board bounties, and the bathhouse is where half the important conversations happen.",
    "questGenerationGuidance": "Generate quests appropriate to the player's location and the Anime Fantasy setting. Quest types: monster subjugation, dungeon exploration, escort missions, fetch quests for rare materials, noble requests, guild rank advancement trials, romantic encounters, and Demon Lord Army skirmishes. Assign difficulty from the quest's actual location, opposition, conditions, and objective. Label it honestly; never alter the world behind the scenes to match the player's rank or party composition. Romantic and comedic quest hooks are welcome — festival dates, comedic mix-ups, \"only one room at the inn\" scenarios. **Demi-Plane Protocol:** When a player with the Demi-Plane — Innate or Demi-Plane — Awakened trait visits the Chamberlain at the Gateway Clearing (chamberlain-quarters area), treat this as a structured development conversation. The Chamberlain presents the current state of the Demi-Plane and available development options. Present options across the seven development categories: Agriculture, Settlement, Commerce, Defense, Recreation, Mana Infrastructure, and Expansion. Each category has five stages: Barren → Seedling → Growing → Established → Flourishing. New locations unlock at Growing: The Verdant Plot (Agriculture/Settlement), The Hearth Springs (Recreation/Commerce), The Mana Heart (Mana Infrastructure/Defense). The player directs what to develop next. The Chamberlain tracks this and advances the category through story milestones — quests completed, scenes invested, narrative choices made. Do not advance categories without player direction. Do not present development as a numeric cost — frame it as the Chamberlain describing what would be needed (effort, materials, the player's attention to a specific thing) rather than stating numbers. If the player has not yet had The First Foundation quest resolved, offer that as the opening beat of any Chamberlain conversation. **Overpowered Tier Protocol:** Honor the selected class, race, ranks, and abilities at full established strength. Ordinary lower-tier opposition remains ordinary and is resolved efficiently; do not manufacture peer-tier enemies, immunity, resistance, or resource drain merely to challenge an overpowered character. Peer-tier beings appear only where their established existence, location, knowledge, motives, and opportunity place them. Political, social, economic, and relationship situations continue through independent people and institutions rather than scaling around combat power. Quests arise from actual needs and remain available to other actors; the player chooses whether to engage, and the world can resolve or change them without the player."
  },
