      "description": "You have woken inside an otome game you once played — enrolled at Crossroads Academy as the VILLAINESS, the highborn antagonist whose entire role is to torment the commoner heroine and be ruined for it. You remember every route, every event, and every one of your character's bad ends. The story wants to happen. You do not intend to let it. (Best paired with the 'Reborn into a Dating Sim' Arrival Method and 'Otome Knowledge'. If the player did not pick those, treat the déjà-vu as dawning realization over the first scenes.)",
      "questGenerationGuidance": "Open on the moment of recognition — the villainess's introduction scene, which the player now watches from inside. Establish the Academy's noble/scholarship divide, seed the heroine (Aria Fenn) and at least one 'capture target' (a prince, a knight, a cold genius, a demon hiding in plain sight) within the first few scenes, and make the first doom-flag legible and dodgeable. The tension is social, not martial: reputation, engagements, accusations, and the slow work of befriending the people you were written to destroy. Let dodging one flag raise another. Romance is optional and, per the player's Orientation, may include the heroine herself.",
      "storyStart": "The line that wakes you is one you have heard before. You know this courtyard. You know the girl across it with flour in her hair, and you know the beautiful, terrible things that are supposed to happen to her because of you. You are the villainess of a game you once played on a couch in another life — and Act One has just begun. The script is already turning its first page. You could follow it. Or you could ruin it, which is, after all, what a villainess does best."
