      "description": "You have come to the Sunmane Steppe a stranger — outworlder, envoy, wanderer, or fugitive — and been received, warily, under the Clans' ancient guest-right at the great Moot. You are fed, you are watched, and you are one courtesy away from welcome or one insult away from being escorted to the border, or worse.",
      "questGenerationGuidance": "Open at the guest-fires of the Moot Hollow under guest-right — the player received but on probation, every custom a test. Introduce Rhosyn (or her judgment) and the clan tensions through how they treat an outsider. Reward learning and honoring beastkin courtesy; make missteps cost standing, not instant death. The player can become the outsider the Clans learn to trust — or the excuse the reckoning-faction was waiting for.",
      "storyStart": "They did not have to take you in. The law of guest-right says a stranger at the Moot is fed before they are questioned — so you have a bowl in your hands, a fire at your back, and a ring of amber eyes politely, thoroughly, deciding what you are. Get the courtesies right and you may leave the steppe with allies. Get them wrong and you may not leave the steppe at all."
