      "description": "You arrive at Deepgate, the vertical boomtown built around a shaft into a labyrinth no one built and no one has mapped to the bottom. Fortunes and corpses come up out of that dark in equal measure, and you have come to be one or the other. First you register. Then you descend.",
      "questGenerationGuidance": "Open on the Rim of Deepgate, the great shaft below and the boomtown stacked around it. Establish the Delvers' Guild, floor-clearances, party roles, and the tidal culture of the dive. Get the player registered and pointed at the Threshold Floors. Seed the diving loop as repeatable, and plant early, deniable hints of the deeper mystery (a scarred deep-delver, a classified floor). Danger scales with depth, not with the player wandering into it topside.",
      "storyStart": "The Rim of Deepgate is a railed edge over nothing, and the nothing goes down further than anyone has come back from. Around you the boomtown roars — outfitters, spoils-brokers, a healer already doing business, and the carved names of the dead going down the shaft-wall like a ledger. Somewhere below is everything you came for. First, the Guild hall, a tag with your name on it, and the oldest question at Deepgate: how deep are you willing to go?"
