      "description": "The theoretical ceiling of mortal spear mastery, achieved by one person per generation at most — and sometimes not achieved at all. The Spear Saint has passed beyond technique into something the martial academies do not have a category for. They do not merely thrust; they impose their will on the space between themselves and their target. Distance is not protection — it is a zone they control. Approach is a calculated risk; retreat is a foregone conclusion. Where the Sword Saint dominates the immediate circle and the Bow Saint dominates the visible horizon, the Spear Saint dominates the killing zone where most combat actually happens. Other S-rank fighters recognize the gap without being asked. The title is not granted by any institution — it is recognized, reluctantly, by everyone who has seen what the holder can do and has survived to report it. Also called Spear Maiden (feminine-presenting) or Lance Sovereign (if neither fits). All three names refer to the same class. Class abilities: Horizon Pierce, Sky-Striding Step, Impaling Aegis, Spear Domain. Narrative note: Spear Saint combat is defined by absolute control of distance and reach. Enemies recognize that they cannot safely approach and cannot safely retreat — the engagement range is the Spear Saint's weapon. Against truly legendary opponents (S-rank monsters, divine entities, other mythic-tier beings), the Spear Saint is challenged but not overwhelmed. Against anything below that tier, they are simply not in danger.",
