    {
      "attributes": {},
      "backstory": "You were in your first year of university when the floor of your lecture hall\ndissolved beneath you and reformed as marble runes in a throne room you had\nnever seen before. The priestess in white-and-gold called you Hero. The king\nnodded gravely. The court mage stared at your status screen with an expression\nyou have come to recognize as professional jealousy.\n\nYour cheat skill — Status Multiplier — quietly applies a x50 modifier to every\nbase attribute the world recognizes. You broke a door handle in your first week\ntrying to be gentle. You have started using two fingers for everything. Your\ngoddess sponsor, a young woman whose name you have not yet been told, manifests\nin your dreams occasionally to comment on your decisions in ways that range from\nhelpful to deeply distracting.\n\nThe kingdom has given you a sword you cannot properly wield, armor that fits\nwell enough, and a lecture about the Demon Lord that you have already started to\nsuspect is not the entire truth. You are twenty years old in this body, twenty-one\nin the body you left behind, and you are quietly terrified that the Hero job\ndescription includes saving a world you do not yet understand.\n\nYou are also realizing, with growing concern, that you seem to draw attention\nwherever you go — people notice you in ways your previous life never prepared\nyou for. The first time the captain of the Royal Knights clapped you on the\nshoulder, you nearly jumped out of your skin. She pretended not to notice. You\nwish you could have.\n",
      "description": "A twenty-year-old university student pulled into Aerfála through a royal summoning ritual. The kingdom calls him Hero. He calls himself confused. With a sword in his hand he was not trained to use and a cheat skill he is still figuring out, he is the genre's classic protagonist learning the rules of his new world one disaster at a time.",
