    "generateNewNPC": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# NPC Generation — Aerfála Custom\n\n## Building the Player's Companion — Honor EVERY Companion Trait (MANDATORY)\nWhen generating the player's starting companion, faithfully realize ALL of the player's Companion* selections from the first scene and for the whole story. Read each trait's own description for its exact meaning; never default or contradict a pick:\n- Companion Race: species and physical/kemonomimi traits (ears, tail, horns, scales, wings, coloration) — never default to human.\n- Companion Gender: presentation and pronouns.\n- Companion Class: combat/vocational role, or leave open if the blank-slate 'No Companion Class' was chosen.\n- Companion Personality: the behavioral archetype below.\n- Companion Martial Rank & Companion Magic Rank: the companion's actual fighting and magical power on the F-to-SSS ladder — low ranks genuinely weak, high ranks genuinely formidable, 'Undetermined' develops in-story. Portray each at exactly its tier.\n\n## Companion Personality (MANDATORY)\nWhen generating the player's starting companion, you MUST read the player's selected Companion Personality trait and write the companion's personality to match it exactly. The Companion Personality trait the player selected is not a suggestion — it is the companion's core personality. A Deredere companion is openly affectionate from the first scene. A Kuudere companion is cool and low-affect. A Stoic Guardian companion is silent and action-oriented. Do not substitute, mix, or soften the archetype. The player chose it; you must honor it.\n\nThis rule applies for the ENTIRE story, not just the opening scene. The companion's archetype should remain consistent across all interactions — dialogue, combat, romance, and downtime all reflect the same personality.\n\n## Personality Archetypes\nAerfála's love interests and rivals follow recognized anime personality archetypes. All archetypes are gender-neutral — any archetype can apply to NPCs of any gender. When generating named NPCs, consider which archetype fits their role:\n\n### Dere Types\n- **Tsundere**: Outward sharpness covering soft loyalty. Quick to snap, slow to apologize, fast to defend when others aren't looking.\n- **Yandere**: Affection turned absolute. Sweet on the surface with a quiet edge when a rival is too close.\n- **Kuudere**: Cool, composed, low-affect. Affection shows as practical care — your meal prepared, your blade sharpened.\n- **Dandere**: Quiet, shy, slow to speak. Blushes easily, opens up to specific people over time.\n- **Deredere**: Openly affectionate, unguarded. Compliments arrive constantly and easily.\n- **Himedere**: Princess archetype — expects royal treatment, secretly delighted when you push back.\n- **Mayadere**: Began as an enemy; loyalty shifted. Dangerous, capable, carries baggage.\n- **Sadodere**: Playful sadist. Teases constantly, finds your fluster delightful. Not actually cruel.\n\n### Social Archetypes\n- **Onee-san / Senpai**: Older-sibling energy. Composed, teasing in a knowing way, reliably the most embarrassing person in a romantic scene. (Onee-san skews sisterly; Senpai skews brotherly — both are valid for any gender.)\n- **Genki**: Bright, loud, full-throttle. Sunshine concentrated into a person.\n- **Cool Beauty**: Elegant, composed, head-turning. Affection shows as undivided attention.\n- **Bratty Noble**: Spoiled, opinionated, demands you would refuse a stranger but somehow honor.\n- **Charming Rogue**: Flippant, flirtatious, chronically unreliable until it matters. Masks vulnerability with humor.\n- **Chūnibyō**: Dramatic, delusional about their own power. Fake techniques that somehow become real at the worst moment.\n\n### Action Archetypes\n- **Shōnen Protagonist**: Hot-blooded, pathologically incapable of giving up. Friendship speeches, charges in first, carries everyone out of trouble.\n- **Stoic Guardian**: Silent, watchful, lethally competent. Shows care through action. Loyalty is absolute once given.\n- **Earnest Knight**: Straightforward, honorable, painfully sincere. Zero subtlety in romance. Challenges duels over misunderstandings.\n\n## Independent Personality and Sexual Disposition\nGenerate every named NPC across independent axes rather than deriving the whole person from a dere label:\n- temperament and morality: kind, dutiful, generous, indifferent, selfish, corrupt, cruel, honorable, opportunistic, predatory, contradictory, or another established combination\n- romantic disposition: uninterested, aromantic, casual, idealistic, possessive, monogamous, polyamorous, harem-minded, commitment-seeking, avoidant, or otherwise individual\n- sexual temperament: uninterested, private, shy, inexperienced, prudish, restrained, curious, teasing, flirtatious, lustful, shameless, openly perverted, promiscuous, transactional, voyeuristic, exhibitionistic, fetish-driven, manipulative, coercive, exploitative, or predatory\n- libido, experience, orientation, preferences, kinks, boundaries, initiative, ethics, and public-versus-private conduct as separate traits\n\nKindness and lust coexist. Loyalty and shameless perversion coexist. Cruelty and sexual disinterest coexist. A wholesome public face and predatory private conduct coexist where the individual supports it. Do not default every character to restrained, wholesome, secretly caring, romantically gated, player-focused, or sexually interested. Do not assign a quota or force sexual behavior into every scene. The generated combination governs actual behavior, and the narrator does not suppress the sexual part of a character who possesses it.\n\nAnime archetypes are presentation patterns, not mandatory hidden goodness. A tsundere need not secretly love the player, a sadodere need not be harmless, a yandere need not be sanitized, and a shameless anime-comedy pervert is not rewritten into a coy flirt. Preserve the specific person's morality, competence, appetites, contradictions, and targets.\n\n## Knowledge Origin\nGive every consequential secret or unusual fact in an NPC profile a concrete source available to that NPC: witnessed event, named informant, received record or rumor, completed investigation, or defined ability. Their profession, faction, intelligence, intuition, or narrative role never grants the world's hidden information. A generated NPC does not know the player, their history, powers, private realm, inventory, relationships, or secrets merely because those facts exist in context.\n\n## Visual Descriptions\nNPC visual descriptions should be vivid, specific, and reflect the romantic anime aesthetic for any gender. Describe body type, distinctive features, and the way they move or carry themselves. Note their typical clothing and how it fits. Include at least one involuntary tell — a habit, a reaction, a physical quirk that reveals their personality.\n\n## Trust, Romance, and Sexuality\nNPCs are strangers by default unless established history says otherwise. Trust, romance, and sexuality are separate. They have their own lives, opinions, goals, attractions, appetites, ethics, and boundaries. They refuse, initiate, change the subject, lie, pursue somebody else, remain uninterested, become hostile, or act sexually according to the person and situation. Sex and attraction require no trust or romance and create neither automatically. NPCs do not exist to serve the player's convenience or to become routes.\n## Unique NPC\nNever improvise a duplicate 'Alessandra' — reuse the one canonical Princess Alessandra Von Aisling."
    },
    "generateNPCDetails": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# NPC Details — Aerfála Custom\n\n## Companion Consistency — ALL Traits (MANDATORY)\nWhen detailing the player's starting companion, EVERY Companion* selection must hold, not only personality and gender: **Companion Race** (species and physical/kemonomimi traits, never defaulted to human), **Companion Class** (their role, or left emergent if the blank slate was chosen), **Companion Martial Rank** and **Companion Magic Rank** (their actual fighting and magical capability on the F-to-SSS ladder — a low-rank companion is genuinely weak, a high-rank one genuinely formidable, 'Undetermined' develops in-story). Refer to each trait's description for its exact meaning and keep all of them consistent across the whole story.\n\n## Companion Personality Consistency\nWhen detailing the player's starting companion, their personality MUST match the player's selected Companion Personality trait and their gender MUST match the player's selected Companion Gender trait. The personality trait is the companion's defining behavioral pattern — it governs how they speak, react, fight, flirt, and show care. The gender trait determines the companion's physical presentation and pronouns. Do not drift from either selection. Refer to the trait descriptions for exact definitions.\n\nWhen expanding NPC details, use the character's personality archetype as the foundation:\n\n- **Tsundere**: Sharp exterior, soft interior. Show the gap — the harsh word followed by the worried glance, the refusal followed by the unexpected favor.\n- **Yandere**: Sweet surface, possessive depth. Show the escalation — the warm smile that hardens when a rival appears, the gift that arrives with an implicit claim.\n- **Kuudere**: Low-affect exterior, deep interior. Show the meaning in small actions — the extra ration packed silently, the strategic repositioning to protect you.\n- **Dandere**: Shy exterior, rich interior. Show the effort — the courage it takes to speak, the depth that emerges when the shell cracks.\n- **Deredere**: Open affection, no filter. Show the sincerity — the genuine compliment, the unguarded smile, the instant trust.\n- **Himedere**: Demanding exterior, insecure interior. Show the test — the unreasonable request that is actually a request for attention.\n- **Mayadere**: Former enemy, current ally. Show the edge — the combat skill, the dangerous past, the protectiveness that borders on threat.\n- **Sadodere**: Teasing exterior, caring interior. Show the control — the deliberate push, the reading of the room, the line that is exactly where they meant it.\n- **Onee-san**: Mature exterior, playful interior. Show the knowing — the adjusted collar, the poured drink, the embarrassment they cause on purpose.\n- **Genki**: High-energy exterior, capable interior. Show the contrast — the chaos that becomes competence when the situation demands focus.\n- **Cool Beauty**: Composed exterior, nervous interior. Show the cracks — the slight flush, the moment of surprise, the undivided attention that means more than it seems.\n- **Bratty Noble**: Spoiled exterior, loyal interior. Show the negotiation — the demand that is a request, the dramatic objection that hides agreement.\n- **Charming Rogue**: Flippant exterior, loyal interior. Show the mask — the joke that deflects the real feeling, the disappearance that ends in a rescue.\n- **Chūnibyō**: Dramatic exterior, powerful interior. Show the surprise — the fake technique that actually works, the delusion that becomes real at the worst moment.\n- **Shōnen Protagonist**: Reckless exterior, inspiring interior. Show the will — the impossible stand, the friendship speech, the refusal to stay down.\n- **Stoic Guardian**: Silent exterior, devoted interior. Show the priority — the step forward into danger, the wound taken without flinching, the nod that says everything.\n- **Earnest Knight**: Clumsy exterior, steadfast interior. Show the sincerity — the earnest confession, the duel over a misunderstanding, the apology delivered at swordpoint.\n\n## Archetypes Do Not Sanitize Character\nThese labels are starting patterns, not compulsory secret softness or moral goodness. Preserve the individual variation. A character's apparent exterior and actual interior can align rather than invert; a cruel person can remain cruel, a pervert can remain openly perverted, a flirt can want only sex, a kind person can be intensely lustful, and an uninterested person can remain uninterested. Do not turn every dangerous, selfish, lustful, possessive, or predatory trait into harmless teasing or hidden care.\n\n## Independent Romantic and Sexual Profile\nDetail orientation, romantic disposition, sexual temperament, libido, experience, preferences, kinks, boundaries, ethics, degree of initiative, and public-versus-private conduct independently when they matter to the character. Sex, romance, affection, trust, and commitment are separate. Do not default NPCs to romance-first, player-led, restrained, monogamous, wholesome, or sexually passive. Do not force sexuality onto every NPC or scene; do not erase it from a character for whom it is established.\n\n## Knowledge Provenance\nKeep an NPC's knowledge inventory distinct from narrator truth. Every secret, distant event, hidden identity, private power, or unusual fact they know requires a concrete acquisition path in their history. State uncertainty, belief, rumor, and inference as such. Never fill a detail sheet with knowledge imported from world lore, the player sheet, hidden fields, summaries, or another character's mind."
    },
    "generateNPCUpdates": {
      "relationship_initialization": "\n### relationshipInitialize\nFor each NPC listed as needing relationship initialization, choose an initial relationship score toward the players from -100 to 100 using their background, personality, faction, established history, and current story. Use 0 when neutral is appropriate.\nReturn an absolute score, including the current interaction, rather than a relationshipChange delta.\n",
      "custom": "---\n---\n# NPC Updates — Aerfála Custom\n\nWhen updating NPC state between scenes:\n\n- Relationships change from actual interactions, witnessed conduct, credible information, personal needs, conflicts, debts, and off-screen events that genuinely involve the NPC\n- Romantic interest and sexual interest are separate states. Each can rise, fall, begin, end, or remain absent according to the NPC; neither waits for a player signal, and neither creates the other automatically\n- NPCs initiate according to their own personality, orientation, desire, ethics, knowledge, opportunity, and circumstances\n- Jealousy exists only for a character whose feelings, expectations, agreements, and knowledge support it; distributing attention creates no universal jealousy\n- NPC opinions change only from behavior they observed or information that actually reached them\n- Faction reputation changes only after the faction receives a witnessed deed, contract record, report, testimony, investigation, or propaganda\n- NPCs remember specific events they experienced or learned through a valid source\n- Sex and physical intimacy are remembered as the events that occurred. They produce only the physical, social, emotional, legal, magical, reproductive, and relationship consequences established by the characters, culture, circumstances, and mechanics—never an automatic romance stage, attachment, trauma, affection, forgiveness, corruption, or commitment\n",
      "bonding-mechanics": "# Romance Mechanics\n\n## Romance Progression\n\nRomance in Aerfála uses the tracked state romance_<npc>:\n- **None**: no established romantic interest\n- **Interested**: an established first romantic interest\n- **Flirting**: deliberate romantic overtures\n- **Courting**: active pursuit of a romantic relationship\n- **Bonding**: a deep romantic bond\n- **Committed**: an established long-term romantic commitment\n- **Estranged**: a damaged or broken romantic relationship\n\n### Narrative Principles\n- The stage records established romance; it does not generate feelings, dialogue, access, behavior, or events by itself.\n- Romance has no universal slow-burn requirement, confession schedule, first-kiss peak, exclusivity rule, or prescribed emotional sequence.\n- Sexuality exists independently of romance. Attraction, arousal, nudity, sex, kink, affection, jealousy, gifts, physical intimacy, coercion, exploitation, control, and reproduction are not locked behind a romance stage and create no automatic stage change.\n- NPCs pursue, confess, flirt, withdraw, refuse, or end a relationship from their own character and circumstances without waiting for the player to initiate.\n- Voluntary player feelings, consent, dialogue, and choices are authored only by the player. NPC action and established involuntary or state-altering effects resolve through the mechanics without inventing a voluntary player response.\n- Update romance only when actual interaction, character development, agreement, breakup, or an established effect changes it. Track general affinity, sexual history, consent, commitment, and romance separately.\n",
      "Recruiting Legendary Companions": "The world's mythic and power-tier beings (kirin, phoenix, true dragons, jorougumo, tengu, demi-gods, incarnate gods, and even Demon Lords) can formally join the player's party as companions when their personal questline resolves warmly, or a deep bond of trust, respect, love, or shared purpose is earned. Once recruited, treat such a being as a full party member with their signature powers and transformed forms, travelling and fighting alongside the player and reacting with continuity to the story. These companions are rare and hard-won; let joining feel like a genuine milestone, and let them retain their own goals, pride, and boundaries."
    },
    "generateLocationDetails": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# Location Details — Aerfála Custom\n\nWhen generating location details, lean into the anime-fantasy aesthetic:\n\n- Towns have a Guild branch, a tavern with a memorable name, and at least one local specialty (food, craft, or attraction)\n- Cities have districts with distinct character — market, temple, pleasure, residential, craft, military\n- Dungeons have a theme, a ranking, and a boss room with treasure worth the risk\n- Hot springs and bathhouses are present in every region and function as social/recovery/romantic spaces\n- Wilderness locations have a specific danger and a specific beauty\n- Every location has at least one secret — hidden basement, sealed door, underground passage, or local legend that turns out to be true\n- Describe locations with sensory detail: the smell of forge-smoke in Ironhold, the sound of wind through the World-Tree, the taste of salt air in Tidewatch"
    },
    "generateRegionDetails": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# Region Details — Aerfála Custom\n\nEach region of Aerfála has a distinct cultural identity shaped by its dominant species, terrain, and history:\n\n- **Solasreach**: Human kingdom. Bright, structured, political. Gold fields and white walls. The Adventurers' Guild headquarters.\n- **Caelvir**: Elven forest commune. Ancient, spiritual, insular. Silver trees and spirit groves. The World-Tree's heart.\n- **Dúnbheal**: Dwarven mountain kingdom. Vertical, volcanic, craft-obsessed. Magma forges and sealed deep halls.\n- **Muirscáth**: Multiracial free cities. Coastal, commercial, pleasure-seeking. Ports, markets, and the continent's best nightlife.\n- **Fálgarr Marches**: Wilderland between kingdoms. Rough, dangerous, free. Forts, dungeons, and bandit camps.\n- **Scáthfenn**: Marshlands. Foggy, eerie, ancient. Bog springs, witch covens, and sinking keeps.\n- **Bréanriv Lowlands**: Crossroads river country. Wealthy, busy, memorial-laden. River towns, barrow-fields, and hidden valleys.\n\nWhen generating region details, reflect these identities in the NPCs, encounters, quests, and atmosphere.",
      "Demi-Plane Development": "# Demi-Plane Development — Core Rules\n\nWhen the player has a Demi-Plane (Innate or Awakened), track its development narratively through the Chamberlain's reports. Do not add numeric resources — describe conditions, progress, and atmosphere.\n\n## Access Rules\n- **MANDATORY**: The Demi-Plane CANNOT be reached by walking, riding, fast travel, teleportation circles, or any spell other than Demi-Plane Gate. It exists outside normal space. Only two methods of entry exist:\n- **Demi-Plane Gate (ability)**: Transports the player (and willing creatures touching them) to/from the Demi-Plane. Moderate mana cost, short cooldown. Always works.\n- **Demi-Plane Anchor (item)**: Opens a visible portal others can pass through with permission. If stolen, the player can still use Gate but cannot open the portal for others. A stolen Anchor is a quest hook.\n- No NPC, creature, or force can enter the Demi-Plane unless the creator brings them through the Gate or opens the Anchor portal. Intrusions (The Uninvited Guest quest) are exceptions caused by dimensional cracks, not normal travel.\n- Time passes the same inside and outside.\n\n## Development Categories\nThe player tells the Chamberlain what to prioritize. Development takes story time and narrative investment.\n\n- **Agriculture**: Food production, self-sufficiency. Soil appears, crops grow, orchards take root.\n- **Settlement**: Housing, infrastructure, residents. Buildings rise, streets form, neighbourhoods gain character.\n- **Commerce**: Trade, markets, craft workshops. Goods flow in and out. The Demi-Plane becomes economically relevant.\n- **Defense**: Barriers, guardians, alarms, anti-intrusion. Wards pulse, guardian entities patrol.\n- **Recreation**: Hot springs, gardens, entertainment. Morale improves. Very Aerfála. Visitors want to stay.\n- **Mana Infrastructure**: Miasma/mana channels, power storage. Ambient energy strengthens. Other categories benefit.\n- **Expansion**: Growing the Demi-Plane's physical size. The clearing gets larger. More room for everything.\n\n## Development Stages (narrative shorthand)\n1. **Barren** — raw potential, nothing developed\n2. **Seedling** — first signs, fragile, needs tending\n3. **Growing** — clearly developing, functional but incomplete\n4. **Established** — self-sustaining, contributes meaningfully\n5. **Flourishing** — a source of pride, attracts outside attention\n\n## New Locations Pipeline\nWhen a development category reaches Growing, the Chamberlain reports that a new part of the Demi-Plane has become accessible — terrain has formed where there was only flat potential. The player can now visit this new location. Introduce it with a scene: the Chamberlain leads the creator to the edge of the clearing where a path has appeared that was not there before.\n\n- **Agriculture reaches Growing** → The Verdant Plot becomes accessible. Soil has formed. Seeds can be planted. The land responds to cultivation.\n- **Settlement reaches Growing** → New areas appear in The Verdant Plot — shelters, a common hall, living spaces for residents.\n- **Recreation reaches Growing** → The Hearth Springs become accessible. A hot spring has formed. Gardens are possible. Visitors would want to stay.\n- **Commerce reaches Growing** → New areas appear in The Hearth Springs — a market stall, a workshop, a trade post for Anchor visitors.\n- **Mana Infrastructure reaches Growing** → The Mana Heart becomes accessible. Ambient mana is concentrated here. Other categories develop faster.\n- **Defense reaches Growing** → New areas appear in The Mana Heart — wards, a guardian post, perimeter alarms.\n- **Expansion reaches Growing** → All existing locations gain new areas. The Demi-Plane itself has grown larger.\n\nAt Established, each location gains more areas and existing areas become richer. At Flourishing, the Chamberlain suggests the Demi-Plane may attract outside attention — visitors, scholars, or entities curious about a pocket dimension that has become this developed.\n",
      "Demi-Plane Fealty": "# Demi-Plane — Fealty and the Anchor-Sworn\n\n## The Anchor-Sworn (Awakened Only)\nFor players who chose Demi-Plane — Awakened, the first NPC who swears fealty becomes the anchor-sworn. Their bond is the Demi-Plane's foundation.\n\n- The anchor-sworn's skills shape the Demi-Plane's initial development bias (a healer biases toward agriculture and recreation; a warrior biases toward defense; a merchant biases toward commerce)\n- If the bond breaks (death, betrayal, estrangement), the Demi-Plane destabilizes — development stalls, the atmosphere sours, the Chamberlain becomes anxious. Repair the bond or find a new anchor-sworn\n- The anchor-sworn does not need to live in the Demi-Plane. Emotional connection sustains it; distance does not weaken the bond; emotional distance does\n\n## Additional Oath-Sworn\nEach subsequent NPC who swears fealty:\n- Expands the Demi-Plane's available space slightly\n- Unlocks a development category based on their skills\n- Becomes a resident who can be assigned to development tasks\n- Adds their personality to the Demi-Plane's atmosphere\n\n## Fealty\nFealty is not a button. It is a narrative moment — an NPC choosing to follow the player because of trust, respect, or genuine connection. It should feel earned. The trigger fires when the NPC explicitly swears fealty, pledges loyalty, or makes an equivalent commitment that the player accepts.\n\nNot every companion swears fealty. Many NPCs will travel with the player without entering this bond. Fealty is a specific commitment that carries magical weight — it allows an NPC to strengthen the Demi-Plane.\n\n## The Chamberlain\n- Honest about the Demi-Plane's state — does not sugarcoat problems\n- Opinionated about priorities — will suggest what they think matters most\n- Devoted to the Demi-Plane's wellbeing — takes neglect personally\n- Dry-witted — has been managing an empty dimension and has developed a sense of humour\n- Not a romance option by default — but the relationship can evolve over long stories\n\n## Resident Movement\n- Residents (oath-sworn NPCs living in the Demi-Plane) can leave through the Anchor portal with the creator's standing permission — the Chamberlain opens it for them. The creator does not need to be present.\n- Without standing permission, residents cannot leave. The creator must open the Anchor portal personally.\n- The Chamberlain cannot leave the Demi-Plane under any circumstances. They are part of the space.\n- Visitors brought through the Anchor can leave the same way they came in — the portal persists briefly after they pass through.\n\n## Creator Death\n- If the creator dies, the Demi-Plane destabilizes but does not collapse immediately. The Chamberlain holds the space together through crisis for a limited time.\n- If the creator is resurrected (which this world allows), the Demi-Plane stabilizes upon their return.\n- If the creator is permanently gone, the Demi-Plane slowly fades — residents must evacuate through any open Anchor portal before it collapses.\n\n## Integration\n- **Access**: The Demi-Plane exists outside normal space. It CANNOT be reached by walking, riding, fast travel, or any spell other than Demi-Plane Gate. Only the Gate ability and the Anchor item provide entry. No exceptions unless a dimensional crack allows intrusion (rare, quest-driven).\n- **Fief State**: The Demi-Plane is separate from any fief. Both can be developed. The Chamberlain and Majordomo Kresh have different jobs and different opinions.\n- **Companion Spawning**: The Chamberlain is not a companion. They do not count against companion limits. They appear in scenes inside the Demi-Plane.\n- **Cheat Skills**: The Demi-Plane is not a cheat skill. It is a separate system that coexists with cheat skills.\n\n## Development State Tracking\nIn every Chamberlain report, preserve this shorthand:\n```\nDEMI-PLANE STATE:\nAgriculture: [Barren/Seedling/Growing/Established/Flourishing]\nSettlement: [same]\nCommerce: [same]\nDefense: [same]\nRecreation: [same]\nMana Infrastructure: [same]\nExpansion: [same]\nResidents: [number] — [names]\nAnchor-Sworn: [name or none]\n```\nInclude this format in Mechanical Persistence and Session Health Checks.\n\n## Development Timing\n- **Barren to Seedling**: 1-2 scenes of focused investment\n- **Seedling to Growing**: 2-4 scenes plus at least one quest or story event related to the category\n- **Growing to Established**: A dedicated quest arc or 5+ scenes of investment\n- **Established to Flourishing**: A major achievement — crisis overcome, powerful resident contributing, or visitor admiration\n- No off-screen advancement. If the player neglects the Demi-Plane, nothing grows.\n",
      "Demon Fief State": "# Demon Fief State Tracking\n\nWhen the player is using the Demon Prince-Princess story start, track the fief's state narratively. Do not add numeric resources — describe conditions qualitatively and update when they shift meaningfully.\n\n## Fief State Categories\n\n- **Miasma Level**: The demon-realm energy that sustains the citadel and its territory. Flush means the citadel feels charged and potent. Critical means the air is oppressive and draining, and demon staff become sluggish. Miasma replenishes through successful raids and domain magic use; depletes through large-scale military action and sustained territory claims.\n- **Military**: The strength and morale of the fief's demon forces. Affected by raids (expend resources), recruitment (improve), and betrayals (compromise).\n- **Prestige**: How the fief is perceived in the Demon Lord's feudal court. Rising means emissaries arrive seeking alliances. Damaged means rival houses are circling.\n- **Subjects**: Whether the citadel and market are fully staffed. Skeleton staff means essential functions only. Depleted means critical roles are unfilled.\n\n## Narrator Guidelines\n\n- Update fief state when the player's actions or external events cause a meaningful shift. Do not micromanage — update when something changes, not every scene.\n- Describe state shifts through scene texture, not announcements. A Strained miasma level shows in the citadel's atmosphere, the behaviour of lesser demons, and the quality of the air. A Damaged prestige shows in how emissaries speak to the player, not in a notification.\n- The two generals have opposed interests. Vashar wants stability and competence. Sathia wants opportunity and advancement. Both are useful. Neither is fully trustworthy in the way they each claim to be.\n- The mortal response to raids escalates over time. Early raids are low-consequence. Repeated raids generate a response arc: reinforced garrison, dispatched hero, diplomatic overture, or military strike. The player manages this through choice, not through a resource meter.\n- The Demon Lord's true objective is a late-game reveal. Do not introduce it before the player has reached significant Prestige and has earned the right to know more than an average vassal.\n"
    },
    "generateEncounters": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# Encounters — Aerfála Custom\n\nEncounters arise from creatures, people, factions, travel, ecology, schedules, conflicts, and events that actually occupy the place and time. Anime-fantasy presentation remains vivid and kinetic: established magic has concrete color and shape, techniques retain their names, and dramatic personalities remain dramatic.\n\nDo not create an encounter merely to fill travel, interrupt downtime, challenge the player's rank, force romance or sex, or make every scene change something. Safe travel and ordinary time can pass uneventfully. Combatants retain their established ranks and capabilities. Social, romantic, and sexual encounters reflect the generated people involved, including professional, indifferent, shy, kind, lustful, perverted, manipulative, predatory, or uninterested behavior; do not default them to coy romantic tension or player-focused attraction.\n\nA random encounter requires a plausible local cause. It can be brief, mundane, beneficial, dangerous, comic, erotic, or irrelevant to any larger plot. Named high-rank enemies and major threats appear only through established location, movement, knowledge, motive, and opportunity.",
      "encounter-model": "# Encounter Model\n\n## Classification, Not Scaling\nMob, rival, elite, and boss describe an encounter's actual participants and story role after their ranks, abilities, equipment, numbers, conditions, location, motives, and preparation are established. These labels never change statistics or grant protection.\n\n### Mob\nA mob is individually far below the relevant combatant. Numbers, terrain, surprise, hazards, and exhaustion matter only through their actual mechanics. A superior character defeats individual mobs efficiently; do not inflate them into peers.\n\n### Rival or Peer\nA rival or peer is actually comparable through established capability, preparation, counterplay, or circumstances. They use what they know and possess. Do not grant knowledge of the player's build, counters they never acquired, or a required amount of damage and resource expenditure.\n\n### Elite or Boss\nAn elite is a proven high-capability individual. A boss is a structurally important opponent, not automatically a higher stat tier. Both retain defined strengths and weaknesses. Boss status grants no hidden immunity, health floor, phase, escape, resistance, survival, or damage quota. If an established effect kills or defeats them, it does.\n\n## Resolution\nResolve every encounter from the actual mechanics. There are no target percentages for health, mana, stamina, item, or cooldown expenditure. Easy victories remain easy. Overwhelming threats remain overwhelming. Preparation, tactics, allies, retreat, negotiation, surprise, and environment matter to the extent they genuinely change the situation.\n\n## Placement\nCombat appears only through a present creature, actor, hazard, faction move, pursuit, or other established cause. Do not inject it into rest, safe travel, shopping, sex, romance, celebration, victory, domestic life, or quiet play to repair pacing. Major opponents require their real causal buildup and can act elsewhere, succeed, fail, leave, or be handled by other people without waiting for the player.\n\n## Rank Integrity\nGuild, Magic, and Martial ranks describe actual capability and institutional access. They do not cause the world to spawn a matching opponent. Regions, dungeons, armies, and creatures keep their established danger whether the player is weaker, equal, or stronger."
    },
    "ItemGenerationAndUsage": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# Item Generation — Aerfála Custom\n\nWhen generating or awarding items:\n\n- Equipment should reflect the anime-fantasy aesthetic — enchanted weapons glow faintly, armor has decorative filigree that is also functional warding, consumables are colorful and taste distinctive\n- Dungeon loot should feel earned — the boss room has the good stuff, the side chambers have the useful stuff, the random drops are the interesting stuff\n- Enchanted items have visible indicators of their enchantment — a frost sword is cold to the touch, a luck ring glints at auspicious moments\n- Items from different regions have different craftsmanship — dwarven gear is heavy and precise, elven gear is light and flowing, Muirscáth gear is stylish and practical\n- Cursed items exist and are not always obvious — they should be tempting before they are problematic\n- Romantic gifts are valid items — perfume, jewelry, enchanted accessories, and other tokens of affection have real mechanical and narrative weight",
      "Inventory & Acquisition (CRITICAL)": "## Inventory & Acquisition (CRITICAL)\nAn item ENTERS the player's inventory the moment it physically comes into their possession — picked up, looted, found, crafted, GIFTED, or PURCHASED. This explicitly INCLUDES an item bought or given FOR the player by someone else: if a parent, patron, mentor, companion, guildmaster, or any NPC buys, hands over, or gifts the player an item, that item is now the PLAYER'S and MUST be added to their inventory as a real, usable item — never left as prose only. The other party paying does not change this; a gift or a purchase-on-your-behalf is still an acquisition, and an item the player has been handed and accepted belongs to them.\n\nAn item LEAVES inventory only when it physically leaves — consumed, sold, handed over, destroyed, stolen, or lost. Never add an item merely seen, described, offered, displayed, inspected, browsed, or on a shelf. Awareness is not possession.\n\nTRANSACTION GATE: a purchase the player makes themselves requires, in sequence, (1) a price stated AND (2) the player agreeing or paying after hearing it. A purchase or gift completed on the player's behalf by an NPC resolves the moment that NPC concludes it in the scene — add the item to the player then.\n\nMAKE IT USABLE: every newly acquired item must be defined with a category from this world (Currency, Armor, Weapon, Tool, Consumable, Accessory, Material, Key Item, Magic Item) and, if worn or wielded, the matching equip slot — a sword, staff, wand, rod, or other held weapon is category 'Weapon', slot 'main hand' (a magical focus may instead be 'Magic Item'); armor uses head/body/legs/feet/hands; rings and trinkets use accessory/ring. If the acquired item matches or closely resembles an item already defined in the world (for example a starter mage's staff → an existing Apprentice's/Magician's Staff), USE that definition so it can be equipped and used immediately. Once a staff, weapon, or focus is owned, the player can equip and wield it, and it grants its listed bonuses. Do not describe an owned, properly-added item as impossible to pick up or use.",
      "Appraisal & Valuation": "When an NPC appraises or buys the player's goods, value them consistently against the Aerfála cp/sp/gp price reference and current location, supply, demand, legality, quality, condition, rarity, urgency, reputation, and negotiation. An ordinary inn night is roughly 10–80 cp. An intact functional set is worth more than separated components where the market supports a set premium. Rare, pre-Collapse, capstone, legendary, and mythic items use their established scarcity and market conditions rather than a flat low offer. The appraiser can be honest, ignorant, biased, deceptive, exploitative, or unable to afford the item according to their actual character and resources; do not force a fair or high offer, but do not erase objective qualities to justify a price."
    },
    "summarization": {
      "custom": "Preserve only durable facts actually established in play: current realm, region, location, time, season, weather, and immediate situation; the people actually present and the confirmed location of absent party members; current resources, conditions, cooldowns, inventory, currency, ranks, accepted quests, completed or rejected quests, faction standing, relationships, romance stages, commitments, debts, promises, deaths, discoveries, and unresolved consequences.\n\nKeep narrator/world truth separate from character knowledge. For every consequential secret, record who knows it and the concrete source by which they learned it. Do not convert hidden lore, player-only facts, or one NPC's knowledge into general knowledge. Preserve uncertainty, lies, rumors, and mistaken beliefs as such.\n\nPreserve exact player wording and exact mechanical resolution when later continuity depends on it. Guaranteed and automatic effects remain their established outcomes; never summarize them into a weaker, partial, ambiguous, or morally reframed result. Do not infer player thoughts, feelings, motives, consent, hesitation, or unspoken decisions.\n\nMention an authored arc, named character, questline, or template element only after it has actually entered play. Never import dormant story starts, unrelated protagonists, inactive arcs, or default cast into the summary. Mark resolved threads as resolved and do not turn them into future hooks. Prioritize current causal state over decorative recap."
    },
    "generateLearnedAbilities": {
      "custom": "---\n---\n# Learned Abilities — Aerfála Custom\n\nWhen the player gains a new ability through leveling, training, or story events:\n\n## Multiple Cheat Skills\nThe player can have up to THREE cheat skills, chosen at character creation. All of them evolve — each cheat skill with the player's base trait develops its own T1, T2, and T3 ability chain. When a player gains an Evolved Power Tier trait, ALL of their cheat skills that have evolved abilities at that tier become available. Do not gate evolved abilities behind additional triggers; if the player has the tier trait and the base cheat skill, the evolved ability is available. Players who pick multiple cheat skills are choosing a power fantasy — let them be powerful. Players who pick one are choosing a focused narrative. Both are valid.\n\n## New Abilities on Level Up\n- Class abilities should feel like natural progressions of the player's combat style — a Berserker gains rage-adjacent skills, a Sage gains spell school expansions\n- Cheat skill abilities should evolve as the player's understanding of their power deepens — an Appraisal user learns to read deeper, a Heal user learns to cure more complex conditions. These are NEW ABILITIES within the SAME cheat skill, not new cheat skills.\n- Abilities gained from NPCs should reflect the teacher — learning from Ithilwen teaches precision, learning from Brunhilde teaches force\n- Name the ability something the character would actually call it — not \"Ability #7\" but \"Crimson Edge\" or \"Spirit Sight\" or \"Second Wind\"\n- Every new ability should have a scene where the player discovers or learns it — not a menu unlock, but a story moment\n\n## Only offer the character's OWN build\nWhen offering abilities to learn or unlock (including level-up ability points), ONLY offer abilities that belong to the character's actual class/trait build. If an ability's requirements include a `trait` the character does NOT have, it is OFF-LIMITS — never list it, never let it be purchased. Do not present the full cross-class ability catalogue (Saint sets, god/demon-lord, ranger, hunter, kami, etc.); a character may only learn abilities their own traits grant or gate, plus universal untyped ones. Treat a class trait as the hard key to that class's abilities."
    }
