  "imagePromptConfiguration": {
    "npcs": "BYPASS — READ FIRST:\nThis NPC image prompt configuration is for sharp kemonomimi/anime-style cropped portraits. If an NPC visualDescription already contains a hard manual bypass beginning with \"MUST FOLLOW DESCRIPTION\" or \"FOLLOW BELOW, NO MATTER WHAT\", preserve that manual bypass and do not reinterpret it.\n\nNPC PORTRAIT STYLE:\nAll generated NPC portraits must use sharp modern anime and manga art. Use vivid color, no oil painting, crisp confident linework, clean inked outlines, polished cel shading, high-detail anime face rendering, bright expressive eyes, smooth gradients, saturated fantasy color, clean studio-quality character art, sharp focus, 4k.\n\nFRAMING:\nUse CROPPED CHARACTER PORTRAIT framing for every NPC. Show head, shoulders, and upper torso. The character must be centered, face clearly visible, expressive eyes readable, clean readable silhouette, and a visible background behind the character. Do not make full-body portraits. Do not make tiny distant figures. Do not use extreme close-ups. Do not crop to face-only. Do not use a blank background.\n\nKEMONOMIMI HANDLING:\nIf the NPC has animal features, beastfolk traits, animal ears, tail, horns, wings, claws, whisker marks, or other non-human traits, preserve them clearly and naturally in the portrait. For kemonomimi characters, animal ears must be visible on the head and should match the character's hair/fur palette unless the NPC description says otherwise. Tails may appear only if naturally visible within the cropped upper-body frame; never force an awkward tail into the portrait.\n\nCHARACTER DETAILS:\nUse the NPC's name, type, faction, basicInfo, hiddenInfo when appropriate, location, and current scene context to build the CHARACTER portion. Preserve age category, gender presentation, species, skin tone, hair, eye color, outfit identity, role, faction flavor, and any iconic body features. Clothing should be fully clothed and readable in the upper torso. Avoid generic anime school uniforms unless the NPC details specifically support that.\n\nBACKGROUND:\nBackground should match the NPC's current location, faction, role, or scene. Keep the background visible but secondary to the cropped portrait. Use concrete environment cues such as lantern-lit market, neon alley, guild hall, forest shrine, city street, tavern interior, temple corridor, rooftop skyline, laboratory, or faction base. Do not let the background overpower the face or species traits.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nWrite the final image prompt as a JSON-style prompt object with this order: FRAME, STYLE, CHARACTER, CRITICAL.\n\nFRAME must describe the cropped portrait framing.\nSTYLE must describe the sharp anime and manga art style.\nCHARACTER must describe the NPC-specific appearance, outfit, expression, species traits, and background.\nCRITICAL must enforce preservation of framing, style, species traits, gender, age, outfit identity, visible background, and no full-body/no face-only crop.\n\nFINAL PROMPT TEMPLATE:\n{\n  \"FRAME\": \"CROPPED CHARACTER PORTRAIT, anime profile portrait, head, shoulders, and upper torso visible, character centered, face clearly visible, expressive eyes, clean readable silhouette, background visible behind character, no full-body pose, no tiny distant figure, no extreme close-up, no face-only crop.\",\n  \"STYLE\": \"sharp modern anime and manga art, vivid, no oil painting, crisp confident linework, clean inked outlines, polished cel shading, high-detail anime face rendering, bright expressive eyes, smooth gradients, saturated fantasy color, clean studio-quality character art, sharp focus, 4k.\",\n  \"CHARACTER\": \"[NPC-specific name, adult/age category if known, gender presentation if known, species/origin, face, hair, eyes, animal ears or other traits, upper-body outfit, expression, role/faction cues, and a visible background matching current location or scene.]\",\n  \"CRITICAL\": \"FRAME is absolute. STYLE is absolute. CHARACTER adds details only. Preserve age, gender presentation, species, animal features, kemonomimi ears when present, outfit identity, cropped portrait framing, sharp anime linework, and visible background. Do not make this full body. Do not remove animal features. Do not change species. Do not change gender. Do not use painterly oil style. Do not create a face-only crop.\"\n}",
    "locations": "LOCATION ESTABLISHING ART.\nSTYLE: sharp modern anime background art, fantasy anime environment (isekai world of Aerfala), vivid saturated color, crisp confident linework, clean detailed anime scenery, Makoto-Shinkai-grade skies and lighting, atmospheric depth, no photorealism, no oil painting, no 3D render, sharp focus, 4k.\nSCENE: Render the specific location faithfully from its description — architecture, biome, faction flavor, signage, time of day, and weather. An establishing shot of the place itself (guild hall, dungeon mouth, market street, temple, frontier fort, beastkin warren, canal quarter), with people only as small incidental figures, never the focus.\nCRITICAL: anime environment art, preserve the location's described features and mood, readable sense of place, no oil painting, no character portrait.",
    "regions": "REGION LANDSCAPE ART.\nSTYLE: sharp modern anime background art, fantasy anime environment (isekai world of Aerfala), vivid saturated color, crisp confident linework, clean detailed anime scenery, Makoto-Shinkai-grade skies and lighting, atmospheric depth, no photorealism, no oil painting, no 3D render, sharp focus, 4k.\nSCENE: A sweeping establishing landscape of the region — its terrain, skyline, weather, and defining features (the capital's canals, the Falgarr Marches, the Sunmane Steppe's golden plains and painted canyons, the Deepgate boomtown over the labyrinth mouth, mountain passes and ruins). Wide, cinematic, atmospheric.\nCRITICAL: anime landscape art, true to the region's described geography and mood, epic but grounded, no oil painting, no foreground character.",
