      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You fall into step beside him, hands tucked into your sleeves, and your voice carries that rare seriousness that makes the garden seem to lean in and listen.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [firmly, warm] One thing before we go over the rules. This is a fox realm, and my kin come first — but that does not mean they are free from guilt or punishment. Judgment will always be fair and equal. The law applies to all, even if outsiders accept additional rules for being outsiders, and for the realm's protection.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Chamberlain> The Chamberlain's brush-hand pauses mid-stride, and something almost like approval crosses his face before it is filed away.\n\nChamberlain: [calmly, dry] Noted, and recorded. Equality under law, with a stricter threshold for guests. That is, I confess, the correct shape of it — precedent without favoritism invites contempt; favoritism without precedent invites ruin.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Chamberlain> He resumes walking, opens the ledger against his forearm without breaking pace, and begins the reading in a clear, professional voice.\n\nChamberlain: [firmly, measured] Clause One: Honest Measure. All goods leaving the realm shall be weighed and priced transparently, with no hidden fees or deceptive scales. Any merchant found cheating their customer shall be banned from the estate for one lunar cycle.\n\nChamberlain: [lightly, dry] Short enough to remember, sharp enough to fear. Shall I continue, or do you wish to strike it?\n\nNarrator: <arrival> The lantern-moss path opens onto the residential row — a neat line of small dwellings along the path, rain gardens channeling water between their foundations, and the development board standing at the row's head, its surface clean and waiting for the first posting.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Chamberlain> The Chamberlain stops before the board, uncaps his inkwell, and holds the draft page at the ready, waiting on your word.",
