      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You turn from the board to the Chamberlain, and your voice stays soft in the way that precedes judgment.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [firmly, cool] Who is this, and why was I not informed that you allowed entry before I brought my kin inside, Chamberlain? Was I not clear before I left?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Chamberlain> The Chamberlain closes the ledger with a soft clap and meets your eyes without flinching.\n\nChamberlain: [calmly, precise] You were clear, Creator, and I did not allow entry. No soul has crossed the threshold. Caspian Vane was not admitted — he was manifested. When the residential row and the records system took root, the realm produced him from its own need, the way the vine produced fruit. He appeared at the development board with ink on his hands and a working knowledge of every ledger I keep. I have questioned him on the realm's history, its contents, and its laws. He knows nothing he was not born knowing, and nothing leaves him.\n\nCaspian Vane: [stiffly formal] Caspian Vane, formerly archivist of the royal records, now sworn to this estate by the fact of my own existence. I did not choose to be here any more than the soil chose to be here. I have entered nothing and left nothing. [dryly] And I would remind you, my lady, that a realm which manifests its own clerks is at least honest about its needs.\n\nChamberlain: [lightly, dry] I confess I did not inform you at once — the matter was uncertain whether it was a person or a feature until he began objecting to my grammar. By then, informing you meant sending word across the threshold mid-journey, and I judged the realm stable. I record the omission as mine, Creator, and take the fault.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Caspian Vane> Vane adjusts the strap of his inkwell and looks down the row of clean, unclaimed dwellings.\n\nCaspian Vane: [precisely] A law without subjects is merely a list of preferences, my lady. I suggest we prioritize the recruitment of a functioning bureaucracy before the first merchant dares to step across the threshold.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Chamberlain> The Chamberlain waits, ledger open, brush poised — ready to commit the vault and the archive to the realm's foundation the moment you give the word.",
