      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> The haze thins as the last demons vanish over the ridgeline. You kneel in the trench mud, wipe the naginata's blade clean with a strip of white cloth, and bind it again with quiet, practiced hands before slinging it across your back.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Taka> Taka flutters down beside you, tilting its porcelain mask toward the thin cut on your forearm. It extends a small paper hand, holding out a folded leaf of healing salve.\n\nTaka: [soft, wordless chirp] Kii.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You let the little construct press the salve into the shallow line across your arm. The sting fades to warmth, and the skin closes beneath its careful ministrations.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike lowers his shield at last, breath coming heavy, and turns a slow circle — counting heads, reading wounds, his fury draining into something grimmer and quieter.\n\nGarrison Sergeant: [gruff, winded] Eyes stay on that ridgeline. They may have run, but ridges lie. Start checking your mates — cuts, bolts, anything bleeding. Nobody hides a wound to look brave. I'll know.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Finnian> Finnian sinks down against the rampart, broken spear across his knees, staring at the two smoking halves of Malrok in the mud.\n\nFinnian: [hoarse, unsteady] We held. Gods above, we actually held.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elian Cross> Cross moves down the line, pulling back gauntlets and peeling sleeves, checking each man's arms and ribs with quick, practiced hands.\n\nElian Cross: [quietly, tight] Gale — show me your side. Don't argue. Show me.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You rise and move back along the trench, laying hands where the salve has not reached — a split brow here, a deep bruise there, warmth flowing from your palms into torn muscle and broken skin until the line stands steadier.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike watches you work, then limps over, shield strap creaking as he tightens it out of habit.\n\nGarrison Sergeant: [gruff, quieter] That's twice today you've pulled my men back from the dark, priestess. I don't know what door you fell through to get here — but I'm not fool enough to look a gift like you in the mouth.",
