      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, honest] I will help while I am able, Sergeant. But I will tell you plainly — my power is not endless. I spent much of it today. What remains, I will spend carefully, and where it does the most good.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, nodding slowly] Honest answer. Rare thing, on this frontier. Most who fall out of the sky promising miracles swear the well never runs dry — right up until it does, with my men standing in the bucket line.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike turns and barks down the trench, one hand still resting on his sword hilt, eyes never leaving the thickening haze on the ridgeline.\n\nGarrison Sergeant: [shouting, brisk] Cole, Ward — east scrub, on the double! Gant, Gale — ford approach, and keep low! Anything moves out there that isn't wearing our colors, you sing out before you stab! Cross — you're with me on the rampart!\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant shoulders his spear with a grim grunt and moves off toward the ford with Gale, both men hugging the trench wall as they go.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Harlan Cole> Cole and Ward scramble east along the parapet, spears leveled, silhouettes low against the smoking turf.\n\nHadrian Pike: [quieter, to you] Here's the shape of it, priestess. They came at us in two waves, planned and patient — that's not a raiding patrol's habit. Somebody spent real soldiers learning what this post can do. If they come back, they'll come back smarter.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He tightens his shield strap, gaze flicking to the two smoking demon corpses in the mud, then back to you.\n\nGarrison Sergeant: [gruff, level] So keep your light for the moments that matter — a warning, a wound, a wall about to break. Don't waste it watching grass. Understood?",
