      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike stops mid-stride, turns back to you, and lets out a sharp breath through his nose. He steps close — close enough that the dented breastplate nearly brushes your sleeve — and his voice drops to a low, gravelly rumble meant for you alone.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, commanding] You're right. You don't know me, and I don't know you. So let me be plain about what this actually is.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, firm] I'm not barking orders at you because of some rank on a scroll. I'm doing it because I'm the only man on this post who knows how to keep you and my soldiers breathing in this hellhole. Twenty-odd years on the frontier, priestess. I've buried men who were faster, stronger, and smarter than me — because they didn't listen to the one holding the shield.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He taps two fingers against his battered shield rim — a dull, hollow knock.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, level] You've got power I can't explain and I won't pretend to understand. Fine. But out here, power without ground-sense gets people killed. So when I tell you where to stand, where to spend your light, when to move — you listen. That's the deal. Not command. Survival.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] You fell out of the sky into a war, and you're still standing. That buys you my respect. It doesn't buy you a free hand to wander this steppe like a pilgrim. Not while there's a second horn out there I haven't accounted for.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, quieter] Now. You wanted explaining — here's the rest of it. This is the Ashen Steppe, the border ground between the mortal kingdoms and the Demon Lord's Army. That patrol that hit us wasn't some rabble — they came in waves, tested our walls, went for the ford. That's Army doctrine. Somebody with rank sent them to learn what this post can do before the next visit comes.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, level] So — questions, priestess. Ask them now, while we've got breath to spare. I'd rather you know the ground than guess at it.",
