      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You tilt your head, tapping your chin with one finger, and let the words come plainly — no courtly wrapping, just honest confusion offered with a small, warm smile.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, candid] Oh. Interesting. So there is a demon lord in this world... Anyways — if I wander this plane like a pilgrim or not is not of your concern, is it? I do not know where you are from or who you serve, but I am no part of that kingdom, no matter which it is. Also, I did not fall out of the sky. I simply stood in burning grass, or whatever that was.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's hand stills on his shield strap mid-tighten. He stares at you for a long beat, the scar across his jaw catching the grey light.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, honest] Anyway — the point is that I could follow the demons, leave the battlefield, or anything else, since I am not bound to any kingdom. So, what deal exactly are you speaking of? Because as I see it, I am currently working for an army I have no loyalties to and no gain from. Not that I want any gain, do not misunderstand, please — but hopefully you see my confusion?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> A dry, short huff of a laugh escapes him — the first sound resembling amusement you've heard from the man all day.\n\nHadrian Pike: [dry, gruff] Ha. A woman with no leash and no price. Do you know what that makes you, priestess? Either the most dangerous person I've met in a decade — or the most honest. Can't decide which, and that's the trouble.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He leans a forearm on the rampart, studying you with the flat, measuring look of a man who has priced every stranger he's ever met.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, level] The deal is simple, then, since you're owed the shape of it. Your expertise — the healing, the light, whatever else you're willing to spend — in exchange for my guidance. How to read this ground, where the cover lies, when the horns mean what. How to survive the Steppe until you find your way back to wherever burning grass spits people out.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, quieter] That's the whole trade. No kingdom, no coin, no colors. You walk when you want. But while you're standing in my trench, you're under my eye — because the Steppe kills the unguided faster than any demon does.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] Fair enough terms? Or does the pilgrim want it in writing?",
