      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You lift a sleeve to your lips, stifling a giggle behind pale silk, eyes crinkling.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [amused, soft] That is amusing, my lord. But I do not need guidance or protection. What I wanted to know — where I am — I know now. The demons do not worry me. But I do appreciate the offer.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike looks at you a long moment, then gives a single, short nod — the kind he gives to a soldier who has stated her piece and will not be moved.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, accepting] Fair enough. I don't need a signature on a scroll, priestess. Just your word and your light — when the line breaks. That's the whole contract.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He steps back from the rampart and sweeps a gauntleted hand toward the haze-shrouded horizon, where the smoke of the ford approach still drifts thin and grey.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, brisk] Deal's struck, so let's use the breath we've got. Gant and Gale are already at the ford approach — and that's where their second wave will want to double back from, once it figures the ridge is spent. The Ruined Ford is the soft way into this post, and somebody over there knows it.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He raps a knuckle against the rampart stone and jerks his chin at Elian Cross, who straightens up from the parapet.\n\nHadrian Pike: [commanding] Cross, on me. Priestess — no obligation, but if you're minded to see the ground before it sees you, the ford's the place. Your choice.",
