      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike pauses at the head of the trench, one boot already turned toward the ford path, and looks back at you with the weary patience of a man who has answered this question around a dozen cookfires.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, level] Kingdom of Solasreach, priestess. Royal frontier garrison — the Crimson Standard flies over what's left of that watchtower, if you care for banners.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He jerks his chin east, toward the grey haze where the ridgeline smolders.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] As for why we're fighting demons in their own territory — that's the question, isn't it. This ground's been contested for longer than I've been alive. Half the old maps call it ours, half theirs, and the Army's decided the argument with arrows every spring since. Twelve years back they stopped coming in force. Everyone called it peace.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, quieter] It wasn't peace. It was them counting. And this year they started counting louder — patrols like that one, moving stones, testing walls. Somebody with rank wants to know exactly how thin we are before the real visit.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elian Cross> Cross falls into step behind Pike, spear gripped tight, eyes flicking to the ridgeline and then briefly — warily — to you before he fixes them forward again.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike sets off along the trench at a steady, purposeful pace, Cross two paces behind. At the trench mouth he glances back once — just once — to see whether the priestess follows.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, over his shoulder] Ford's a quarter mile east, priestess. Gant and Gale are already out there. If you're coming, come now — I don't double back for stragglers.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He does not wait for an answer. The two soldiers' silhouettes dwindle along the trench wall, into the smoke drifting low over the scorched turf, and the choice of the ford path lies open before you — east with them, or nowhere at all.",
