      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You lift two fingers, and your shikigami stir at the unspoken word. Suna rises into the grey air, climbing until the haze swallows her, set to watch the slopes. Hoshi-maru takes station at your shoulder, scanning the perimeter. Genkurō slides ahead of your steps, a paper guardian screening the path. Taka flutters close, brushing ash from your sleeve with fussy little hands.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Finnian> Finnian wipes his spear across his gambeson, watches Pike's silhouette dwindle along the trench, and then falls in behind you with a nervous half-step — a young soldier choosing to shadow the strange priestess rather than stand alone.\n\nNarrator: You follow the soldiers out of the trench, curiosity carrying you where duty carries them. The burnt turf crunches underfoot, and spring's stubbornness shows even here — pale wild rose shoots pushing through scorched ground, one migratory bird wheeling overhead through the smoke.\n\nNarrator: <arrival> A quarter mile on, the ground drops to a shallow, rocky crossing. The water runs grey with ash, sliding over stones the color of old bone. On the near bank, two soldiers crouch behind a broken causeway — Gant with a crossbow braced, Gale flat against a boulder. Pike and Cross come down the slope to join them, and Gant's head snaps up at the sight of your party.\n\nElias Gant: [tense, low] Sergeant. Didn't expect you out here. Ridge quiet?\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, level] Quiet for now. The ford's where they'll want to come back through, so this is where we stand. Gale — anything moved on the far bank?\n\nTiran Gale: [quietly, flat] Crows, Sergeant. And something bigger, maybe. Bushes shifted twice, downriver. Could be wind.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's eyes cut to the downriver scrub, then to you, standing calm at the bank's edge with your paper guardians arrayed like a quiet honor guard.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] Priestess. Since you're here — Gale's spotted movement downstream. Your watchers see anything my men can't, you tell me. That's the whole of it.",
