      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You find a corner of the bank where the ash hasn't settled — a flat stone between two boulders, half-sheltered from the haze. You kneel there in perfect seiza, sleeves gathered, and draw a small lacquer tray, a tin of tea, and a battered iron kettle from thin air.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> The ford's grey water goes into the kettle without complaint. Foxfire licks beneath it, patient and low, and the smell of toasted rice tea begins to cut through the ozone and burning turf.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, agreeable] As you wish.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant's crossbow dips an inch. He stares at you — kneeling, pouring tea, three paper figures standing sentinel around you like funeral guests — then drags his eyes back to the water with visible effort.",
        "Elias Gant: [low, muttering] ...She's making tea. Sergeant. She's making tea.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] I can see that, Gant.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike keeps his position at the causeway, gaze moving between the downstream scrub and your small, absurdly calm ritual. His jaw works once. He doesn't repeat the request — he simply waits, grim and expectant, the strap of his shield creaking under his thumb.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Flat against his boulder, Gale scans the far bank, spear gripped white-knuckle tight. The bushes downriver shift again — and this time the movement has direction, slow and deliberate, upstream toward the ford.",
        "Tiran Gale: [quietly, tight] Sergeant. Downriver again. It's not wind. It's pacing us.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's head turns a fraction. He reads the scrub the way an old hound reads a treeline, then looks back at you — kneeling, serene, steam rising off your cup.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, low] Priestess. Tea can wait or it can't — your call. But if your paper friends see what's pacing my man downriver, I want it now, not after you've finished pouring."
      ],
