      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [dry, mildly amused] Does it look like those three can see what you can't? I doubt it. Also, there is a fourth one, Suna, in the sky keeping watch. If anything was truly approaching, she'd have reported it to me already. So may I have my tea now, or are simple pleasures not allowed in a war zone?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike holds your gaze for a long beat. Then something in his jaw unclenches — not quite a smile, but the ghost of one behind the beard.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] Drink your tea, priestess. Just keep that fourth one's eyes working while you pour.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant mutters something under his breath and re-braces his crossbow on the causeway stone, though his glance keeps sliding back to the steam curling off your cup.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale's head stays low, but his eyes track the downriver scrub. The bushes shift again — closer to the ford now, maybe forty paces off — then stop entirely. The bank goes still.",
        "Tiran Gale: [tight, whispering] Sergeant. It stopped. That's worse than moving.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [low, flat] It's deciding. Gant — cover the water. Cross, watch our back-trail. Nobody fires until I see teeth.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike crouches at the causeway, shield angled toward the grey water, and speaks without turning his head.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, level] Whatever's down there has watched us for a quarter hour and not crossed. Demons don't do that. They come in loud or they come in numbers. One thing, patient, pacing — that's not Army doctrine.",
        "Elias Gant: [grim, quiet] Steppe wolf, maybe. Or one of those half-blood scavengers the caravans talk about. Neither answer's good.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's eyes flick to you, kneeling serene on your flat stone, cup in hand, paper guardians standing watch.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] Priestess. If your sky-watcher sees it cross the water toward us — or if it turns out to be more than one — that's when I'll want you. Until then, sip away."
      ],
