      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Genkurō> You sigh, set your cup down on the lacquer tray, and speak the order softly. Genkurō rises at once, paper spear leveled, and glides down the bank with rhythmic, unhurried precision — a white shape moving through grey haze toward the silent scrub.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hoshi-maru> Hoshi-maru peels away in the opposite direction, flanking wide along the waterline, cutting off the downstream route with stiff, exact strides.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's head snaps around at the movement of your guardians.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, sharp] Priestess — what are they doing?\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [flatly, annoyed] Fetching me whatever has been ruining my tea with all this creeping about. Sit still, Sergeant. If it were an army, you'd already know.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale presses flatter against his boulder, spear raised, as Genkurō reaches the scrub's edge — and stops, spear-point dipping toward the densest tangle of branches.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Genkurō> The paper guardian thrusts once. The scrub erupts.\n\nNarrator: A figure lurches out of the brush and scrambles back — not a wolf, not a demon of the patrol you fought. It stands near seven feet, grey-skinned, gaunt, wrapped in patched hides and ash-stained cloth. Its eyes are mismatched: one molten demon-orange, one dull mortal brown. Its hands are empty, raised high and open. Behind it, Hoshi-maru plants his spear in the shingle, sealing the riverbank retreat.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike rises slowly from behind the causeway, shield up, sword drawn but low.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, wary] Gray-Walker. Half-blood scavenger. They trade on the steppe — sometimes. Gant, keep that bolt on it. It talks, or it dies where it stands.\n\nGray-Walker Scout: [hoarse, urgent, frightened] No blades — no blades, soldier-folk. I carry no iron. I come with word, not war.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, flat] Word from who?\n\nGray-Walker Scout: [hoarse, low] From the stones. The boundary stones in the old garden province — your Army's moving them again. Third night running. And the ones who move them... they wear no general's mark. They wear the mark of House Vael. Your garrison is not being tested, soldier-folk. It is being measured — for someone's private ledger, not the Lord's war.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant's crossbow does not waver, but his eyes cut to Pike, the tic in his cheek jumping.\n\nElias Gant: [grim, quiet] Sergeant — that name's not Army doctrine. That's court politics wearing armor.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, to himself, grim] ...That's what I was afraid of.",
