      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You rise from your flat stone in one smooth motion, sleeves settling, and pour a second cup into a spare bowl from the tray.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, mild] Genkurō, Hoshi-maru. Bring him to me.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Genkurō> Genkurō glides back at once, spear leveled at the scout's spine, herding him up the bank with rigid precision. Hoshi-maru stays planted by the shingle, cutting off the water.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Gray-Walker Scout> The scout comes stiff-legged, hands still open, mismatched eyes flicking between the paper spear at his back and the small woman standing beside a lacquer tray of steaming tea. He stops an arm's length away, unsure whether he's a prisoner or a guest.",
        "Gray-Walker Scout: [hoarse, hesitant] ...You are not soldiers.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] I am not. Sit, if you like. You've been crouched in wet brush for a quarter hour — the tea is fresh, and the bank is no place for hospitality.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike steps forward before the scout can move, shield angled, gaze hard as river stone.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, flat] Hold. You'll drink nothing until you talk. Which stones — names, markers, positions. And how many men did you see wearing Vael's mark?",
        "Gray-Walker Scout: [hoarse, low] The stones of the old garden province — the ones your maps call dead ground. Three moved in three nights, each shifted east toward the trade road. I counted eight men the first night. The second night, twelve. They work in silence, with wagons and chains, and they kill anything that wanders close. My cousin wandered close.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant's bolt stays centered on the scout's chest, his voice a low rasp.",
        "Elias Gant: [dangerously quiet] And if you're lying, half-blood, that bolt goes through your throat before you can blink. So think hard before the next word out of your mouth is a pretty one.",
        "Gray-Walker Scout: [hoarse, urgent] I do not lie to soldiers who hold the ford. Kill me, and the next scout House Vael buys will not speak at all. I came because the Gray-Walkers cannot fight them — we only walk between. You have walls, and iron, and a priestess who pours tea while demons die.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's jaw works. He looks from the scout to you — standing calm beside your tray, second cup steaming, guardians flanking the half-blood like an honor escort.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [low, grim] Twelve men with chains moving boundary stones, and no general's banner over them. That's not a patrol. That's a survey crew for a land grab — and my garrison's sitting on the ledger line.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, to the scout] Who gave you this? A name. Someone in Vael's camp talks, or you'd know nothing.",
        "Gray-Walker Scout: [hoarse, hesitant] ...A quartermaster who hates his paymasters. He sells word for salt and iron, nothing more. I do not give his name to soldiers who might trade it back.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike stares at the scout a long moment, then glances at you — the second cup still steaming on your tray, offered to a creature everyone else in the ford has a weapon trained on.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [dry, grudging] ...Priestess. Your guest. Your call whether he drinks. But every word he said goes in my report, and I want him saying it again while Gant writes it down."
      ],
