      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You lift the iron kettle and refill Talin's cup without a word, watching the steam rise while Pike's question hangs over the shingle. Mana still sits low in you — the morning's foxfire has not yet returned in full — and you weigh that against a half-day's march east.",
        "Talin: [hoarse, grateful] Thank you, priestess.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Talin> He drinks slowly, both hands around the cup, and his mismatched eyes stay on you with a quiet, patient hope.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, flat] Well? The orchard, or the ford. My men don't march on maybe.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, measured] I will come with you to the dry orchard, Sergeant. The stones concern me more than the ford does — and my watchers can guard your rear better than any scrub line. But hear one condition: my mana is spent from this morning's fighting. I cannot call foxfire freely until it returns. If Vael's men find us before it does, you fight, and I do not promise miracles.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] First honest answer anyone's given me all day. Fine. We move at dusk — Vael's crew works in the dark, so we'll be in the dark with them. Cross, Gant, Gale — you're with me. Finnian holds the ford with the wounded.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Finnian> Finnian's knuckles whiten on his notched spear, but he nods.",
        "Finnian: [nervous, steady] I'll hold it, Sergeant."
      ],
