      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I look at Genkurō and Hoshi-maru \"you two stay and assist Finnian until i return or call for you.\" Then i lift my gaze to the sky, alrhough not seeing Suns i speak anyways \"Suna. You stay as well and inform Genkurō and Hoshi-maru about any movement. Work together.\" Then at taka \"and you, little one, move ahead please go and watch. If anything seems off to you before we arrive then you come tell me.\""
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You rise from the flat stone and turn first to Genkurō and Hoshi-maru.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, formal] You two remain here and assist Finnian until I return — or until I call for you.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Genkurō> Genkurō bows with rigid precision and steps to Finnian's side, laying a paper hand on the young soldier's shoulder — a steadying weight, deliberate and unmistakable.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hoshi-maru> Hoshi-maru takes position on Finnian's other flank, spear planted vertical, its white mask sweeping the perimeter in slow, rhythmic arcs.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, upward] Suna. You stay as well, and inform Genkurō and Hoshi-maru of any movement. Work together.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Suna> Suna lifts from the shingle without a sound, circles the ford once, and hangs high above the crossing — a pale fleck against the grey haze, watching everything at once.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> Last, you crouch slightly to meet the small porcelain mask at your knee.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [gently] And you, little one — move ahead of us. Watch the road. If anything seems off to you before we arrive, come tell me at once.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Taka> Taka flutters a small bow, then zips east into the haze, gone between one blink and the next.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Finnian> Finnian exhales a long, shaky breath, staring at the two paper guardians flanking him like a man unsure whether he's been blessed or haunted.\n\nFinnian: [nervous, low] I... thank you, miss. I've never held a line with anything like these before.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, dry] You're holding it with more than most garrisons get, boy. Count your luck and keep your spear up.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant checks the straps on his kit, then glances at the sinking afternoon light — the haze already dimming toward a grey dusk.\n\nElias Gant: [grim, flat] Dusk march, Sergeant. Half a day east means we reach the orchard past midnight, if the ground allows it.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, low] Vael's crew works past midnight too. We'll be quiet company for them. Eat now, check water, and say your prayers — the steppe doesn't forgive a loud boot.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Talin> Talin rises, pulling his ash-grey hides close about himself, and moves to stand near you — patient, silent, waiting on the priestess who gave a name before a question.",
