      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You rise fully and face Talin, hands folded within your sleeves, and bow — a small, proper bow, the kind given between equals.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, sincere] Thank you, Talin. For your cousin's story, for the stones, for trusting strangers with what cost your kinship blood. I do not forget kindnesses received.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [gently] And now — what will you do from here? The steppe is no gentle place for a man walking alone with a secret in his pocket.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Talin> Talin lowers his head, the grey of his face catching the last of the afternoon light through the haze.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, quiet] You gave my cousin a name and a prayer. Few in this ash have done half that. I will not forget it either, priestess.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, steady] My road is this: I walk the shadows with you as far as the markers — I know the ground, where the stones stood and where Vael's men dig. I guide from a distance, where their blades cannot reach. Then I turn west, to my kinships, and warn them. House Vael kills witnesses. My people are witnesses. They must scatter before the new moon.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike, tightening his shield strap out of habit, glances between you and the tall scavenger.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, flat] A guide who won't stand in the fight. Fine. Better than no guide at all — and he moves quieter than any of mine. Just remember, Talin — if the priestess falls, your road ends fast.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, dry] Then I will pray she does not fall, soldier.",
