      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike signals the men to fall in with two fingers, and Elian, Elias, and Tiran form a tight line behind you. He drops his voice to a whisper that still carries command.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, commanding] Gear silent. Eyes on the haze. If you can hear your own boot buckles, you're too loud.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Talin> Talin melts into the grey scrub at the edge of the path, his ashen hides blending until only his mismatched eyes mark him. He moves in a wide, ghostly circle around the column, scouting for Vael's sentries.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You wait through the long grey afternoon, seiza-still on the flat stone, until the sun finally drowns in the haze and the steppe turns to ash-dark. Then you rise, bow once to Finnian, and lead the party out.\n\nNarrator: <arrival> Twelve kilometers of silence pass under your feet — sulfur flats, cracked stone, the hiss of steam vents — before Taka flutters back to your shoulder and points ahead with a tiny paper hand.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Taka> Taka's porcelain mask tilts toward a cluster of geothermal vents, where three gaunt Grey-Walker figures crouch around a piece of dented plate armor, arguing in low, rasping hisses.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's hand closes into a fist — halt. He crouches, shield low, and studies the figures through the steam.\n\nHadrian Pike: [whispering, grim] Three scavengers. Gray-Walkers, like your Talin. Not Vael's men — they'd have killed us already. But they're loud, and loud carries.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant eases down beside him, squinting through the vent-haze.\n\nElias Gant: [grim, low] They're squabbling over salvage. Knight's plate, by the look — someone died out here recently. Could be ours, could be Vael's work.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Talin> Talin materializes at your elbow as if the ground coughed him up, voice barely a breath.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, whispering] Those are Ashkin kinship — distant cousins of mine. Wary, but they trade. Miasma-resistant minerals, good ones. They want food or news from the mortal side. They will not want soldiers near them, though. Your call, priestess — you are the one they might speak to.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike looks at you, jaw tight, steam curling between you.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, low] Your watchers found them, your Talin vouches for them. Do you talk, or do we slip past and lose the hour?",
