      "storyMessage": "Hadrian Pike: [gruff, whispering] Talk, then. But you walk slow and hands open — if they bolt, we lose the lead. If they scream, we lose the night.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> He stays crouched, shield across his knee, and waves his men flat into the scrub without a sound.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, whispering] Stay behind me three paces, priestess. I will raise my hands first — they know the sign of parley. Then you step out where they can see you.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Talin> Talin rises from the scrub like a column of smoke and lifts both long hands, palms out. The three scavengers freeze mid-argument, salvage tool and scrap metal coming up in defensive grips.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, calling softly] Ashkin. It is Talin, of the shadow-walkers. No blades, no soldiers behind me — only a priestess who wishes words and has tea to spare.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 1> The nearest scavenger — yellow-eyed, fingers twitching — lowers his scraping tool halfway and squints past Talin at you.\n\nGray-Walker scavenger 1: [rasping, wary] A priestess? Out here, at night, with armed men crouching in the scrub? That is not a pilgrim, cousin. That is trouble wearing a kind face.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, sincere] I will not argue the armed men — they are soldiers of the Solasreach garrison, and they stay where they crouch. I am Tsukiko, and I only wish to ask what the ash has told you lately. You were found over a dead knight's plate. Who buried him?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 2> The second scavenger clicks his yellowed nails together rapidly, glancing at his companions before answering.\n\nGray-Walker scavenger 2: [rasping, low] Nobody buried him. We found him two days past, east of here, near the old orchard road. Grey tabard, Solasreach make, throat opened clean. No wounds else. And around him — bootprints. Many. They dragged something heavy toward the orchard. We did not follow. Following is how kinship members stop being kinship members.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant's head lifts slowly from the scrub, his nervous tic working in his cheek.\n\nElias Gant: [grim, muttering] Sergeant. A knight, killed quiet, dragged toward the orchard. That's not a patrol skirmish. That's Vael cleaning up after themselves.",
