      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You bow properly — hands within sleeves, a small formal inclination — before stepping closer, the steam thinning around your shoulders.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, sincere] Thank you for what you've told me. And since you've paid me in truth, let me pay you back in kind. If I were to offer you a position under my name — work as your skills allow — what would you ask in return? I do not take what is not given. Talin spoke of his kinship endangered, and so I offer his kin a place beneath my protection. Refusal I will accept with grace. But if you would consider it — tell me your price.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 1> The yellow-eyed scavenger's twitching fingers still. He studies you a long moment, suspicion warring with something sharper behind it.\n\nGray-Walker scavenger 1: [rasping, slow] A position. Under a priestess who speaks for the Gray-Walkers. If my kin are safe — truly safe from the Vael fires — I would ask a sanctuary where the ash does not choke the lungs, and grain that does not run out. But tell me honest, priestess: do you have such a place? Or are you buying loyalty with promises?\n\nGray-Walker scavenger 2: [rasping, rattling laugh] Sanctuary! You are a bold one. My price is simpler, priestess. Gold enough to buy out my debts to the scrap-lords of the flats — and a guarantee that if we serve you, you strike the Vael wherever they hide. Do that, and my blade and my eyes are yours.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 3> The third says nothing. His gaze slides between you and Talin, tongue clicking once — then he lowers his rusted salvage hook to the ash, a slow, deliberate signal that he is listening.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Talin> Talin's mismatched eyes fix on you, and something tight in his tall frame eases.\n\nTalin: [hoarse, quiet] She has a place. I have seen its gate. Ask her nothing she has not already proven, cousins.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> From the scrub, Pike's rasp cuts low and flat.\n\nHadrian Pike: [whispering, warning] Careful, priestess. You're hiring scavengers in a war zone — they'll follow the gold until the wind shifts. Don't promise a paradise you can't build, or they'll sell us to Vael the first blind spot we hit.",
