      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, honest] I promise only what I can hold. I will not speak of where the place is — not yet, not here, where the ash carries words to the wrong ears. But there is a place of safety, for you and your kin, if you are accepted. Talin has seen its gate; I will not oversell what he has already confirmed.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, measured] Know this also: service under my name is bound by riddle-craft, the same binding I laid upon another who serves me now. It forbids lies against me, harm to me and mine, and false faces. It binds me as much as it binds you — I do not take what is not given. Weigh it. Accept or refuse, and I will take either answer with grace.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 1> The yellow-eyed scavenger turns the words over, fingers still. He looks at Talin, then at the paper fox perched on your shoulder, and something in his sunken face settles.\n\nGray-Walker scavenger 1: [rasping, slow] A binding that cuts both ways. That is more honesty than the scrap-lords ever offered. I am Ronan. If the gate is real, I will walk through it and see for my own eyes before I swear my kinship to it. That is my condition — not refusal.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 2> The second scavenger laughs his dry rattle and slings his scrap metal across his back.\n\nGray-Walker scavenger 2: [rasping, wry] Urix will follow Ronan, because Urix has no ideas of his own. But my price stands, priestess — the Vael, struck where they hide. Bind me to your riddle-craft and I will count your enemies' boots and mark their fires. Call me Syril. I would rather serve a shrine that keeps its word than die neutral in the ash.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Gray-Walker scavenger 3> The third — Urix — clicks his nails once and nods, saying nothing, but he steps in behind Ronan's shoulder. Chosen, by silence.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike rises slowly from the scrub, sword still loose in its sheath but his hand never far from the hilt.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, flat] Congratulations, priestess. You've doubled our mouths to feed and tripled the number of people who can sell our route to Vael. Ronan — you walk where I can see you. Syril, anything you hear from my men goes to her first, or the binding won't be your biggest problem.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant mutters into his collar, spear still angled at the newcomers.\n\nElias Gant: [grim, muttering] Gold to desperate men in a wasteland. Nothing's ever gone wrong with that. Sergeant, we burning the night on this, or moving?\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, commanding] Moving. Ronan — you know this ground. Where do those bootprints from the dead knight run, and how far to the orchard road?",
