      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You smile softly, falling in behind the point line.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, calm] Riddle-Craft has not been used yet. But it will be — once I fulfill their conditions and they decide whether they accept my offer or not. Until then, we are companions in honor. Now let's go, so we can get this done quick.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elias Gant> Gant grunts, shouldering his spear, and falls into column without another word.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ronan> Ronan takes the lead toward the basalt pillars, each step placed with deliberate care. He signals with two fingers — step where I step — and the column follows his prints exactly, the ground between his footfalls glowing faintly with heat.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Syril> Syril slides into the staggered line, nose lifting into the wind with a slow, rhythmic sniffing, tongue clicking softly when the sulfur gusts shift.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Urix> Urix hugs Ronan's shadow, eyes darting between the cracked crust and the soldiers' leveled spears, silent as falling ash.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike keeps the pace steady, his gaze cutting between the three scavengers ahead and his soldiers' spacing, tightening his shield strap out of habit.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, gruff] Eyes open, all of you. Half a night's march to the orchard road. Nobody strays from the prints.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> Your bioluminescent markings bleed soft light through the dark as you walk — Pike shoots you one flat look, and you dim what you can, the glow refusing full subtlety.",
