      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: [OOC Summary] You are Tsukiko Kuzunoha, the veiled Mother Fox — an ancient nine-tailed kitsune walking Aerfála in mortal guise, SSS-rank in magic and martial arts, currently mana-depleted. After a long string of deeds — salvaging a wagon, binding the shade Zeryth, exposing the embezzler-murderer Corvath Salt before Bréanriv's council and distributing his 6,100-gold hoard to the victims' families, and developing your hidden Demi-Plane estate with its Chamberlain, border protocols, and fox-masked attendants — you were diverted to a frontier hillside in the Ashen Steppe, where you helped Sergeant Hadrian Pike's garrison repel a Demon Realm patrol, healing the wounded and killing several demon raiders. A captured Gray-Walker scout, Talin, revealed that House Vael is secretly moving boundary stones in the old garden province to shift the miasma-line and seize trade roads, killing witnesses — including a knight found with his throat slit. You recruited three Gray-Walker scavengers — Ronan, Syril, and Urix — under a promised \"riddle-craft\" binding, while Talin departed west to warn his kin. Your company is now crouched in the dark above the Low-Silt Wash, having spotted a formal demon gathering below: a ring of sentries around a pillar of white light, silk-sashed nobles at the center, drilled soldiers in ranks, and ragged bond-laborers at the rim. Pike must choose between a risky sneak through the basin's rear edge or a long detour over thin, superheated crust, before the ceremony ends. Your current task points toward a formal demon social encounter — a Virtue Court — where you must participate correctly or exit without insult.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Ronan> Ronan crouches low, long fingers twitching as he studies the basin's rear edge, then leans toward Pike.",
        "Ronan: [rasping, low] Rear edge is a mess, Sergeant. Sulfur vents and shifting shale — unstable, loud, one wrong step and the whole wash hears us. But... the shadow of the western ridge runs clean along the rim. Stay under it, single file, and we slip past the sentry line without the silk ever seeing us.",
        "Hadrian Pike: [low, gruff] Under the ridge shadow, single file, past a demon court's back door. Fine. Ronan takes point. Cross, count our paces. Priestess — keep that paper fox of yours low and quiet. We move on my fist."
      ],
