      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You tap your chin, moonstone eyes on the white glow bleeding up from the basin, and turn to Pike.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, calm] Sergeant? May I approach them? I have questions I wish to ask — and it may help us pass without bloodshed.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike's head snaps around. For a heartbeat he just stares, then his hand leaves his shield strap and pinches the bridge of his nose.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, flat] Approach. A silk-sashed demon court. Alone. On the night we nearly died at the ford.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [gently] I am not alone, Sergeant — I have my foxes. And a court is a place of rules. If they are demonstrating a Virtue for inspectors, then protocol protects a guest who comes openly. A squad crawling through their rear edge does not.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadrian Pike> Pike looks at you — the ruined gambeson soldiers behind you, the exhausted scavengers, the basin full of silk and steel — and his jaw works slowly.\n\nHadrian Pike: [gruff, reluctant] Damn it. She's right, and I hate it. A formal court can't cut down a guest without insulting the inspectors watching them. That's armor better than any breastplate.\n\nElias Gant: [grim, muttering] If they follow the rules. If one sash decides a fox-woman isn't a guest but a trophy, no protocol saves her.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, flat] Then we don't let her stand alone. Gale, Cross — with the priestess, ten paces back, spears down. Rest of you hold the ridge shadow. Priestess — you walk out where they can see you coming, hands open, and you say nothing I wouldn't say. If a single sword clears a scabbard, you fall back and we take the long way. Agreed?\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] Agreed.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale's knuckles whiten on his notched spear, but he crawls to your side, voice barely a breath.\n\nTiran Gale: [whispering, tight] Ten paces back, ma'am. Just — don't stop walking toward them, whatever they say. I've heard courts like that like confidence.",
