      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You rise from the ridge shadow, leave your spear-women where they stand, and walk out alone into the open, hands empty and visible, your foxfire marks glowing faintly against the dark — a beacon no one on the rim can mistake for stealth.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale and Cross trail you at ten paces, spears angled down, Gale's shoulders shaking with every step while he forces his eyes forward instead of at the sentries.\n\nHadrian Pike: [low, muttering] Walk slow. Count your steps, priestess. If a blade clears leather, you drop and we run.\n\nNarrator: The sentries see you long before the light does. A horn does not sound. Instead, a tall demon in grey-and-white sash steps out of the perimeter, blade sheathed, and studies you the way one studies weather — then gestures, almost courteously, for you to follow him through a gap in the ring.\n\nNarrator: The basin opens into something far older than a campsite: a court of silver-wood architecture grown out of dark stone, a white spire of light rising from a polished floor, and around it the machinery of ceremony — adjudicators with bone tally-staves, silk-sashed nobles of House Vael, bound laborers kneeling at the rim with their eyes on the ground. The Vael knight who met you speaks without turning his head.\n\nVael Herald: [dry, formal] A guest arrives unannounced at a demonstration of Pride. Bold. Or foolish — the adjudicators will decide which. Come. You will wait in the envy-alcoves until the floor is finished, and you will not speak until spoken to. That is the Threshold of Propriety, honored or broken.\n\nNarrator: <arrival> He leads you beneath a carved lintel into a side gallery — the envy-alcoves — where niches of silver-wood line a dim corridor and the murmur of the Pride-floor filters through like surf. Other petitioners wait here: a scarred demon merchant tallying grievances on a slate, and a gaunt half-blood with chained wrists who watches you with hollow, calculating eyes.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> Gale and Cross halt at the alcove mouth, spears grounded, both visibly out of their depth. The herald plants himself beside the lintel like a doorpost.\n\nVael Herald: [flatly] The alcoves are for grievance and negotiation. Whatever you are — priestess, soldier, or something stranger — you will be assessed before the court's business concludes. Sit. Wait. The Virtues are patient, and so must you be.",
