      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You incline your head to the herald — acceptance given without a word — and settle into one of the silver-wood niches in seiza, spine straight, hands resting in your sleeves. From your Item Box you draw the lacquer tray, iron kettle, and tea tin, and begin the quiet work of tea as though the court's noise were a garden stream.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> At the alcove mouth, Gale has gone rigid, spear grounded, eyes snapping between the herald's back and you with every small motion of your hands.\n\nTiran Gale: [whispering, barely audible] Ma'am — is — is making tea in a demon court allowed?\n\nNarrator: The herald glances once, says nothing, and returns his gaze to the corridor.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadriel Dusk> Across the gallery, the chained half-blood shifts his weight, iron links whispering against stone. His hollow eyes track your every gesture — the tray, the kettle, the unbothered stillness of your posture — measuring, recalculating what you might be.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Balthazar Grimm> The scarred merchant's stylus stops clicking. He leans toward you, voice dropped beneath the murmur of the Pride-floor.\n\nBalthazar Grimm: [low, sardonic] Patience is a virtue, but in this court, it's often a mask for desperation. Keep your eyes on the adjudicators, not the tea, if you intend to leave here with your skin intact.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You pour the first cup without looking up, steam curling past your face, and set it on the tray — silent, exactly as promised.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Balthazar Grimm> The merchant watches the pour, then the faint glow of your markings, and his scarred mouth twists — half suspicion, half grudging interest. His stylus resumes its slow click against the slate, but his eyes stay on you between glances at the corridor.\n\nNarrator: Somewhere beyond the lintel, the Pride-floor's murmur rises and falls like tide against the silver-wood walls. The adjudicators' tally-staves tap in slow rhythm. No one calls for you yet.",
