      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You lift one finger to your lips — no word, just the gesture — and the two soldiers at the alcove mouth go still as cut stone. Then your attention returns to the kettle, the pour, the slow curl of steam.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale stands frozen, knuckles white on the notched spear. He swallows hard and glances at Cross, eyes wide and pleading for some sign they aren't about to be executed over a cup of tea.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elian Cross> Cross shifts half a step, putting his dented cuirass between Gale and the corridor. His eyes sweep the gallery — the herald, the merchant, the chained half-blood — and he chews the inside of his lip, saying nothing.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hadriel Dusk> Across the gallery, the chained half-blood leans back against the silver-wood wall, iron links clinking softly. His hollow eyes follow the steam rising from your tray with a hungry intensity — weighing whether you are a fool to be ignored or a power worth using.\n\nHadriel Dusk: [low, hoarse] Tea. In a demon court. Either you know something the rest of us don't, woman... or you've already decided how you want to die.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Balthazar Grimm> The scarred merchant snorts at that, stylus pausing mid-click.\n\nBalthazar Grimm: [sardonic] Mind your chains, Dusk. She poured before anyone spoke to her — that's not madness. That's someone who's read the Threshold better than you have.\n\nNarrator: Beyond the lintel, the Pride-floor's rhythm changes — the adjudicators' tally-staves stop tapping in unison, and a voice like struck slate calls out across the court.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Vael Herald> The herald turns from the lintel, his thumb flicking once against his blade's hilt, and looks down at you.\n\nVael Herald: [dry, formal] The floor concludes. The adjudicators will receive petitioners from the alcoves in order of arrival — and you, guest, arrived before either of these. Finish your tea. Then stand, and follow 