      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> The herald leads you into the Pride-floor's open light without once looking back, his pace measured and rhythmic, each step placing you exactly where a guest is meant to stand.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale fixes his eyes on the back of your robes and follows with stiff, mechanical precision, breathing shallow, vibrating with every tap of the adjudicators' staves.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Elian Cross> Cross drifts a half-step wide, covering Gale's flank, his gaze cutting between the gallery shadows and the silk-sashed nobles filing in around the floor's rim.",
        "Narrator: The Pride-floor opens around you like a held breath — the white spire of light burning at its center, adjudicators seated in a crescent of bone and silver-wood, and above them all, on a raised perch draped in black silk, a figure watches with the lazy attention of a cat that has not yet decided whether to play.",
        "Lilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, carrying across the floor] A mortal. Uninvited. With tea on her breath and soldiers at her heel. How... novel. Approach the crescent, little lantern, and let us see what Pride finds worth measuring in you.",
        "Vael Herald: [dry, formal] You are received. Speak when the Empress permits it — and not before."
      ],
