      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You cross the Pride-floor at the herald's measured pace, unhurried, and stop where a guest is meant to stand — ten paces from the crescent of bone and silver-wood.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale keeps his head bowed low behind you, grip tightening on the spear until his knuckles crack. He makes himself small, a soldier trying to become furniture.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Elian Cross> Cross drifts a half-step to put his dented cuirass between the Empress's perch and Gale. He does not move again, but his eyes tick from exit to exit, counting paces.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> On the Observer's Perch, the Empress leans forward, chin settling into a manicured hand. Black silk slides from one pale shoulder. Her gaze comes down the length of the floor like a blade laid flat against skin — patient, amused, waiting to see which way you break.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid] No trembling. No bow deep enough to grovel, none shallow enough to insult. You walked in here like the floor was built for you.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> At the crescent's end, Dorian Vael stands rigid, thumb flicking once against his hilt, slate-grey face betraying nothing as he studies you.\n\nDorian Vael: [dry, formal] Guest. State your name, your trade, and the road that brought you across House Vael's ground. The court will judge whether the crossing was courtesy or trespass.\n\nNarrator: The adjudicators' tally-staves rest silent in their laps. The spire of light at the floor's center burns steady. Every eye in the court waits on you — and the Empress's smile widens by a single, deliberate degree.",
