      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale makes a small, strangled sound behind you — the noise of a man watching someone juggle live coals.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian Vael goes rigid from collar to heel. His eyes narrow to slate slits, and when he speaks, his voice has dropped to something glacial and precise.\n\nDorian Vael: [glacial, formal] I am the Voice of Protocol in this court. The herald speaks for the Empress's silence; I speak for the law's questions. To confuse the two is to admit your own confusion, guest. You will answer what is asked — or be judged a trespasser who lacks the wit to understand her own predicament.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Above, the Empress laughs — soft, melodic, entirely delighted. Black silk slides as she leans further over the perch railing, chin in hand, looking at you the way a collector looks at a piece she has decided she wants.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, delighted] Oh, Dorian, do be a dear and stop boring her with your ledgers. She caught the seam in your orders in front of my whole floor — do you know how long it's been since anyone dared? I find her appetite for contradiction far more appetizing than your etiquette.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> A muscle ticks in Dorian's jaw. He does not reply to her. His thumb flicks once against his hilt — harder than before — and his gaze returns to you, colder and more interested than it was.\n\nNarrator: The adjudicators exchange a look. One tilts his tally-stave, marking something — though whether against you or for you, the floor cannot say.",
