      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You let the Empress's laughter pass over you like weather, keeping your eyes on the slate-grey officer. Your voice comes soft and even, the tone of a woman correcting a mislabeled ledger.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] I asked a clear question. Flourish words will not change your avoidance of answering it. Are you the Empress? Yes or no? If the answer is no, then do not tell me to speak only after she permits it — you are not she. That is not a confusion of mine, but a failure of yours. My wit is perfectly fine. Your orders are not.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> The floor goes silent. A long moment passes — then Dorian Vael, slowly, deliberately, lifts his hand from his hilt and straightens his collar to a knife-edge of posture. The glacial annoyance in his face melts into something rarer: keen, professional curiosity.",
        "Dorian Vael: [dry, measured] ...No. I am not the Empress. You are correct on every count, and I will not pretend otherwise before my own adjudicators. So — since you find my orders flawed, guest, you are welcome to propose a corrected protocol for your own questioning. Provided you can do so without further insulting the structure of this court.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Above, the Empress purrs — a low, rolling sound of genuine humor. She shifts her weight on the perch, black silk sliding, her eyes fixed on you with a collector's hunger.",
        "Lilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, amused] Dorian, dear, you should be grateful. She's teaching you the difference between a rule and a wall. — Tell me, little lantern... do you intend to dismantle the rest of my court's dignity as well? I do so hope the answer is yes.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Behind you, Gale shudders visibly, breath hitching in a thin whistle. His spear-tip trembles against the floorboards — a man watching the executioner's axe rise and hoping it is aimed elsewhere."
      ],
