      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You tilt your head, unhurried, and let your gaze climb the perch to the Empress herself.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] That depends. Are other parts of this court as inconsistent as your Voice of Protocol? If so, I would naturally speak my mind when I witness such failure — as I did just now. A court only works if its officials know their place and abide by their own rules. Contradictions only lead to problems no one wants.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> The Empress hums — soft, melodic, a note of genuine approval. She shifts on the perch, black silk sliding, and her gaze traces you from heels to hair with open, predatory curiosity.",
        "Lilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid] Mm. A well-ordered court is a boring court, little lantern. What I find far more delicious is the sight of someone actually capable of enforcing one. Tell me — do you enforce, or merely lecture?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian holds his rigid posture, but the glacial coldness in his eyes has thawed into something rarer — a flicker of professional respect.",
        "Dorian Vael: [dry, measured] Your logic on consistency is sound, guest. But understand: this court's value lies in its stability, not its perfection. Rules survive because they bend without breaking. — So I ask you plainly: do you believe a few inconsistencies justify dismantling an entire legal structure?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> Gale lets out a shaky, audible breath, knuckles whitening on his spear. He leans a fraction toward your back, voice a strangled whisper.",
        "Tiran Gale: [whispering, desperate] Lady Tsukiko — please — stop poking the demons. Please.",
        "Narrator: <focus:adjudicator 1> The pale adjudicator with the four-pupiled eyes makes one sharp, definitive mark on his tally-stave. He leans forward, head tilting left, watching your reaction to the Empress's hunger with clinical detachment — a man recording something for a ledger that is not the court's."
      ],
