      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You tilt your head, faintly puzzled, as though the question were a child's riddle.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] Naturally, I'd accept. Although I have no reason to prove anything to you, I also have no reason to hide. Your abyss is just another of many. And in the end, all are the same — and none has ever shaken the foundation of what I have.\n\nNarrator: <focus:adjudicator 1> The pale adjudicator makes three rapid, precise marks on his tally-stave, four pupils dilating in unison as he records your words. His head tilts further left, listening to something only he can hear.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> The Empress beams — a slow, widening curve of delight, her eyes narrowing to slits of molten amusement. She rises from the perch rail, black silk cascading.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, pleased] Such confidence. A rare vintage in my court, little lantern — most who drink it are dead before the second sip. I look forward to seeing whether that foundation of yours is as unshakable as you claim. The Abyssal Testing Grounds will tell us both.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> A short, dry huff escapes Dorian Vael — the closest thing to laughter his posture has permitted all evening. His rigid shoulders ease by a fraction.\n\nDorian Vael: [dry, measured] Confidence bordering on insanity. Though I will grant, guest, that insanity is often the only thing that survives the Testing Grounds. I have seen sanity buried there more times than I can count.\n\nTiran Gale: [whispering, horrified] Lady Tsukiko — you can't — we're in the heart of the demon realm! Please, reconsider — they'll tear the words right out of you down there, I've heard what happens in these places, please—\n\nNarrator: <focus:adjudicator 1> The pale adjudicator leans toward the Empress and speaks for the first time, his voice a dry whisper of falling ash.\n\nadjudicator 1: [softly] She has declared a foundation, Empress. The Grounds will weigh it. I would suggest... we record everything.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> The Empress waves a hand, silk sleeves rippling, and the gallery lights dim to a warm ember-glow.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid] Then it is decided. Rest tonight, little lantern — the Grounds are not kind to the tired, and I want you at your sharpest. Dawn, at the Descent of Discernment. Do try to keep that foundation intact until then. I've grown fond of it already.",
