      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You wave Tiran silent with two fingers, not looking back, and lift your voice to the perch — soft, unhurried, impossible to mistake for a plea.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] I do not require rest. But my human companions do — a bed, a light meal, if you would be so gracious. And while they are seen to, let us proceed with your test now. I have other matters awaiting me, and I would rather not waste anyone's time. Yours least of all.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> A ripple of laughter moves through the gallery — the court has never heard a guest ask a Demon Lord to hurry. The Empress flicks her wrist, silk sleeves spilling, and two staff demons peel away from the walls at once.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, delighted] Your generosity is as curated as your confidence, little lantern. Granted — your pets shall be fed and rested, so you may have no excuses when your foundation begins to crack. And since you are so eager to spend your evening in my Grounds... who am I to make a fascinating woman wait?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian Vael steps forward and delivers a stiff, formal bow toward the two soldiers — precise to the finger's width.\n\nDorian Vael: [measured] Humans. You will be escorted to the guest quarters. A meal and beds will be provided. You will not wander. — Guards, see them transferred.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tiran Gale> The guards take Gale's shoulders. He exhales a long, shaking breath, and as they lead him toward the silver-wood arch, he twists to look back at you.\n\nTiran Gale: [quietly, awed] ...Thank you, Lady Tsukiko. For the bed. For — all of it.\n\nNarrator: <focus:adjudicator 1> The pale adjudicator makes a single, deliberate mark on his tally-stave, then turns without a word and begins walking toward the Descent of Discernment — an unspoken signal that the test is beginning now, on your terms.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> The Empress descends from the perch in a slow drift of black silk, stopping an arm's length from you — close enough that the heat of her rolls off her skin like a hearth. Her eyes are molten and patient.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, softly] No rest, no excuses, no fear. I have not been this entertained in a decade, little lantern. Walk with me — the Descent is this way, and I do so enjoy a guest who sets the pace.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian falls into step behind the Empress, thumb resting against his hilt, his voice pitched low enough for you alone.\n\nDorian Vael: [dry, quiet] You asked for speed, guest. Be careful. The Grounds answer faster than most expect.",
