      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I look at dorian \"Do you always speak this much? Unasked? When the proceeding is already clear? I do not care how fast the ground answers. Otherwise i would have asked. So if you do not mind - i want to proceed now. And if possible without pointless conversation.\""
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian stops mid-stride. His posture snaps back to full military rigidity, and for a moment the only sound in the corridor is the click of his thumb settling against his hilt.\n\nDorian Vael: [dry, measured] Your appetite for efficiency is noted, guest. But do not mistake brevity for lack of substance. If you wish to bypass the pleasantries — then lead the way. I shall be the one to ensure your speed doesn't carry you directly into a pit you cannot climb out of.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> The Empress glides a half-step closer, silk whispering across the silver-wood floor. Her smile deepens, molten and unhurried.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, softly] I find your disdain for dialogue refreshing, little lantern. It is rare to meet a mortal who treats my court like a tedious appointment. Very well — let us see whether your actions are as concise as your tongue.\n\nNarrator: <focus:adjudicator 1> The pale adjudicator waits at the mouth of the Descent of Discernment, tally-stave resting against his shoulder. He does not invite. He simply stands where the corridor swallows the light.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You fall into step past him without a word, and the tapestries of the Descent come alive around you — their woven figures writhing into shapes drawn from your own thoughts, then settling when you refuse to look at them twice.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian follows at your shoulder, matching your pace exactly, his boots silent on the stone.\n\nDorian Vael: [quietly, dry] The tapestries read you, guest. What they show the adjudicators is not for your eyes. Walk as though you have nothing to hide, or do not walk at all.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> The Empress trails behind like a shadow in silk, her voice drifting down the corridor with lazy warmth.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid] Do hurry, little lantern. The Grounds have been so starved for something interesting.",
