      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You tilt your head, and the temperature of the platform seems to drop a degree.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, coldly] Wasn't I clear? Start. The. Test. Or are you prepared to find out what consequences may find you if you keep testing my patience? Proceed. NOW.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> <hit:intimidate:1> The Verifier's needle fingers stop mid-notation. All four amber eyes widen a fraction — the first crack in his clinical stillness — and the ledger lowers an inch before he catches himself. The mana-siphon beneath the stage pulses once, hard, reacting to the certainty rolling off you like heat off stone.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> Vassago straightens, and for the first time his voice carries something other than precision — a faint, involuntary deference.",
        "Vassago the Verifier: [coldly, measured] ...The terms stand as stated. Your answer is deferred, not refused. First weight begins. Proposition one: all order is a cage, and every cage is built by fear. State whether you agree — or demonstrate that you do not, and be measured by how.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Kaelen the Hollow> The old man leans back, a thin mocking smile touching his translucent lips.",
        "Kaelen the Hollow: [dry, weary] Or was that thunder the sound of a foundation holding — or the hesitation of someone realizing her pride has a price tag? Do answer, mortal. I collect both.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Lilessa watches from her bone seat, chin propped on one hand, pure languid fascination in her molten eyes. She does not intervene. She simply enjoys the spark.",
        "Lilessa the Ashen Empress: [languid, softly] Mm. The lantern flares. Proceed, Verifier — she is already halfway to breaking your ledger, and you have not even asked the hard question yet.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian stands rigid at the platform's edge, thumb still against his hilt, watching you with a dry, critical eye — weighing whether your demand for speed is leadership or merely impatience wearing armor.",
        "Dorian Vael: [low, dry] The Grounds measure deeds, not volume, guest. Answer the weight. The siphon has already recorded your certainty — now it wants your reasoning."
      ],
