      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You don't answer the proposition. You speak the un-word.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Kaelen the Hollow> <hit:208:0> The sound has no shape — a silence that bites. Kaelen's left side simply stops existing: half his vestments, half his ribcage, half his mocking smile gone, replaced by a shimmering absence that hisses where the vortex's light tries to fill it. He staggers, silver hair drifting loose, and catches himself on nothing — still standing, still breathing, half of him present and half of him no longer anywhere.\n\nKaelen the Hollow: [ragged, wheezing] ...ah. So the lantern... burns after all.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You exhale, slow, the mana drain a cold pull through your bones — a price paid in full for a half-measure you chose.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly, coldly] Gods, how I despise people like him. Acting like they know it all while knowing nothing.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> All four amber eyes go wide. His needle fingers stop trembling over the ledger and go still entirely. When he looks up at you, there is something new in his face — clinical terror, worn like fascination.\n\nVassago the Verifier: [coldly, carefully] ...Literal. Short. Honest. How I know of your realm and your words to your Chamberlain: I do not. I know only what this court's instruments recorded of your arrival and what its spies reported of your dealings in the borderlands. Your demi-plane, your Chamberlain's protocols — those I learned of only now, from your own mouth, spoken in this trial. That is all of it. Every word.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Lilessa is on her feet. Not rising — arriving, silk still settling, as though the space between her seat and you was always hers to skip. Her molten eyes never touch the wounded archivist. Only you.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [laughing, low and delighted] Oh. Oh, little lantern. A century of Pride demonstrations and wringing politics, and you are the first thing in this court to make the Verifier's hands shake. I could eat you whole and still be hungry.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian's hand closes around his hilt — not drawing, gripping — and his stance shifts a half-step forward, weight balanced, calculating.\n\nDorian Vael: [low, dry, tightly] You have wounded a guest of the court inside a sanctioned trial. Protocol permits me to treat that as an attack on the court itself. I am electing not to. Be aware that this election has a cost, and you are spending it.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Zeryth> The oil-black mass ripples with a slow, satisfied pulse, its geometric spikes lengthening toward the Verifier like a cat stretching toward a cornered thing.\n\nZeryth: [oil over glass, genderless] Mm. The vacuum is delicious. Do continue.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Kaelen the Hollow> The half-erased old man drags himself upright against a floating shard of obsidian, runes on his ruined vestments guttering. He laughs — thinner now, wetter.\n\nKaelen the Hollow: [dry, rattling] Note it in your ledger, Verifier. She answered the second weight after all. Every judgment of intent... is tyranny wearing kindness... when the judge holds an un-word. You have proven his proposition... by demonstration.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> Vassago's ink-stained finger hovers over the ledger — and for the first time, he does not write. He waits, all four eyes on you, the second weight hanging open in the humming air.",
