      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> <hit:209:0> Your voice drops to something older than the court, and the word you speak is not a word at all — it is permission, and it lands on Kaelen like a verdict. The half-erased scholar convulses as the command tears through what remains of him, his runes guttering out one by one.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [coldly] Zeryth. You may consume Kaelen.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Zeryth> <hit:209:1> The oil-black mass rises off the platform like a wave given intent, iridescent and silent, and crashes over the crawling scholar — engulfing his legs, his ruined side, dragging at what is left of him as he claws at the obsidian.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> <hit:209:2> Steel sings. Dorian is between the wave and the scholar before the ripple finishes forming, his drawn blade shearing a shallow gash through the fluid's leading edge. Zeryth recoils, a ripple of irritation running its surface, the strike leaving a thin scar of light across its black hide.",
        "Dorian Vael: [low, hard] Enough. A guest of the court is under the court's protection — even one the Empress finds amusing. Withdraw, creature, or I treat this as an attack on the realm itself.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Kaelen the Hollow> Zeryth pulls back, sullen, and Kaelen drags himself away from it on two working limbs, leaving a wet smear across the obsidian. He laughs anyway — ragged, wet, delighted.",
        "Kaelen the Hollow: [wheezing, dry] Record it, Verifier... the perfect irony... a god's hunger, sanctioned by protocol's blade... write it... write it all...",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You cross the platform in three unhurried steps and take Vassago by the collar, hauling him down to your eye level. Your moonstone eyes shift — pink-gold fire rising beneath the grey like coals under ash.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [quietly, coldly] I said answer in honesty. And you dare lie to my face? I did never speak of my realm, of what I've spoken about with the Chamberlain, or anything else — before you used it in your second proposition. So tell me. How. Do. You. Know?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> The ledger hangs loose in his trembling needle fingers. All four amber eyes are fixed on yours — the scholar in him trying to file the moment into a category and failing, because nothing in his framework holds a mortal who grabs a Verifier of the abyss by the collar and is not struck down for it.",
        "Vassago the Verifier: [shaking, precise even now] I— the instruments— the court's instruments recorded your arrival, your route, your dealings at the border garrison. The spies' reports. That is the whole of my knowledge. I swear it on the ledger itself. I did not lie. I could not— the Verifier does not lie. It is the one law I have never broken.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Lilessa glides close — too close — silk whispering across the obsidian, her molten eyes drinking in the Verifier's frozen face. Her voice is a purr meant for you alone.",
        "Lilessa the Ashen Empress: [softly, hungry] There it is. His fear. A delicacy I have not tasted in an eternity — and you brew it like tea. Tell me, little lantern... do you intend to erase the rest of my court as well? Because I find I am beginning to hope you might."
      ],
