      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian steps forward, rigid and formal, and closes his gauntlet over your wrist — attempting to pry your grip from the Verifier's collar.",
        "Dorian Vael: [dry, flat] Release the Verifier. Your grievance is noted, but you are disrupting the flow of the trial, and protocol does not permit the assault of an official during a sanctioned weighing.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> <hit:210:0> Reality Touch fires — the world shivers, a half-second where every law of force bows aside, and your free hand moves once. The crack of Dorian's arms and legs breaking is crisp, four reports like green wood snapping. He drops to the obsidian in a heap of charcoal robes, blade ringing loose across the platform, breath driven out of him in a single ragged hiss.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [quietly, coldly] Do not ever touch my servants again, Dorian, or you may be its next meal. Know your place. Do you understand?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Zeryth> You lay your palm on the oil-black mass, and warm light runs through its hide — <hit:210:1> the scar of light across its surface smoothing away, the fluid rippling with restored vigor.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] You may eat now, dear.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> Vassago hangs frozen in your grip, breath hitching, all four amber eyes locked on the burning pink-gold beneath your grey.",
        "Vassago the Verifier: [shaking, precise] If you believe my words are falsehoods... then you are judging me by a standard I do not possess. I speak only what is written.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [coldly, burning] Lies. I have not once spoken about any of this in any place of Aerfála. Last chance, Verifier.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Lilessa watches Dorian's broken form with a languid, predatory smile, making no move to intervene. She leans in, silk whispering.",
        "Lilessa the Ashen Empress: [teasing, soft] Do let him struggle, Dorian. I want to see if our guest intends to break the Verifier's spirit — or simply his neck.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Zeryth> Zeryth slides toward Dorian's heels, mass undulating like a tide, spikes rising and falling in slow hunger.",
        "Zeryth: [oil over glass, genderless] The knight tastes of salt and iron... the Verifier tastes of ink and terror. Which shall we savor first, Master?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Kaelen the Hollow> From the floor, the half-erased scholar coughs a spray of silver blood and laughs — wet, rattling, genuinely delighted.",
        "Kaelen the Hollow: [wheezing, dry] Yes... tear it down... let the ledger burn in the fire of a god's spite... it's the only honest thing this court has ever seen...",
        "Narrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian drags himself onto one working elbow, face grey with pain and something colder — the discipline holding where the body fails. He does not reach for the blade.",
        "Dorian Vael: [low, strained, dry] ...Understood. The fault was mine. Protocol forbade my hand, and I extended it. I will not touch your servants again, guest. Finish your question.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> The Verifier's needle fingers tremble against his ledger. His mind races — the instruments, the spies' reports, the court's records — searching for the loophole in his own testimony, and finding the seam at last.",
        "Vassago the Verifier: [carefully, hoarse] ...There is one source I did not name. The siphon. The mana-siphon above this stage drinks from every soul that stands beneath it — it tasted your memories when you entered the trial. What it drank, the court wrote down. I read what was written. I did not lie. But I did not tell you where the words came from. That omission... is mine."
      ],
