      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I point to kaelen \"Him, Zeryth.\" Then i look at the verifier \"You are playing a dangerous game, verifier. I tomd you to answer honestly. Is omission honest? Yes or no?\" Then i turn my fury towards the siphon."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [coldly, without looking away from the Verifier] Him, Zeryth.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Zeryth> <hit:210:2> The oil-black mass turns like a tide answering the moon. It flows over Kaelen the Hollow in one smooth, inevitable surge — and this time nothing bars the way. The scholar's laughter cuts off mid-breath. What remains of him dims, gutters, and is gone, drawn down into the iridescent dark without struggle, without ceremony, without a name left to mourn. The obsidian where he lay is clean. Zeryth settles back, its surface rippling with slow, sated pulses.\n\nZeryth: [oil over glass, genderless] ...He tasted of dust and unfinished questions. Thank you, Master.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> The Verifier does not move. His ledger lies face-down against his chest, forgotten. All four amber eyes are fixed on the clean stretch of platform where a man used to be.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [quietly, coldly] You are playing a dangerous game, Verifier. I told you to answer honestly. Is omission honest? Yes or no.\n\nVassago the Verifier: [hoarse, shaking, precise even in ruin] ...No. Omission is not honest. It is a lie told by silence — and I have committed it. Record my fault as you will. There is no clause in my law that permits me to argue the point.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You release his collar and let him drop back onto his heels. Then your head turns — slowly — toward the mana-siphon humming above the stage, the vortex beneath it churning with everything it has drunk from you. The pink-gold fire beneath your moonstone eyes rises.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> Vassago scrambles back a half-step on his knees, needle fingers splayed, his gaze darting between you and the humming instrument above.\n\nVassago the Verifier: [whispering, urgent] The siphon is an instrument of the court. To destroy it is to blind the Empress's sight here — every record, every weighing, every secret this stage has ever tasted flows through it. Break it, and the court is deaf.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [laughing, low and delighted] A god who dislikes being read. How delightfully possessive. Tell me, little lantern — does the siphon's hunger match your own? Or will you simply break my pretty eye and pretend you never looked through it?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> Dorian lies broken on the obsidian, arms and legs ruined, and makes no move at all. Only his eyes track you, cold and disciplined, a ruined piece of the court's protocol accepting its place in the wreckage.\n\nKaelen the Hollow: [wheezing, dry] Break it... break the machine... let the abyss finally be blind to us all...\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Lilessa settles back onto her seat, chin propped on one elegant hand, molten eyes glittering — waiting to see whether you shatter the court's eye, or whether the Verifier's confession has bought it a stay.",
