      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I look at the verifier \"stop whining like a brat. Lear to use your ears. I ordered it to erase what it has of me. Nothing else. So stop annoying me.\" I look at Lilessa \"if we're done here, i've had enough of people talking unasked, people not listening, people speaking nonsense after i already explained. I expected a test and not to be annoyed. I'm done here unless you can finally get your people properly under control and do their tasks as intended.\""
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You look down at the Verifier, still flat on the obsidian, and your voice is flat as slate.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [coldly] Stop whining like a brat. Learn to use your ears. I ordered it to erase what it has of me. Nothing else. So stop annoying me.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Vassago the Verifier> Vassago stays where he fell, needle fingers still spread against the stone, voice trembling but clinical.\n\nVassago the Verifier: [hoarse, precise] ...The records are gone. Your existence is once again a mystery to the court. I have no more information to withhold, and no more weights to present. I am merely a witness to a vacuum.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Dorian Vael> A short, pained huff escapes Dorian — almost a laugh, if his crushed chest allowed it.\n\nDorian Vael: [low, strained, dry] Efficient. You've broken the limbs of the guard and the memory of the court. If you intend to leave, do so now, before the Empress decides that a blank slate is the perfect place to write a new, more permanent contract.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Lilessa the Ashen Empress> Lilessa rises from her seat at last, silk sliding across obsidian, and glides toward you — close enough that the heat of her rolls against your skin. The amusement has sharpened into something genuinely hungry.\n\nLilessa the Ashen Empress: [softly, intent] The board is wiped clean and the court is blind. A perfect silence. If you're truly done with my nonsense, little lantern, then let us see what remains of the test when the rules are gone. Stand your ground — or leave this place, and I shall spend the next century wondering how I lost the most interesting thing I ever found.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You turn your eyes to her, pink-gold banked low beneath the grey, and let the silence sit exactly as long as it pleases you.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [quietly, coldly] If we're done here, I've had enough of people talking unasked, people not listening, people speaking nonsense after I already explained. I expected a test — not to be annoyed. I'm done here, unless you can finally get your people properly under control and do their tasks as intended.",
